1
00:00:05,547 --> 00:00:07,549
[wind howling]

2
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:16,558
[footsteps approaching]

3
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,039
[hinges creak]

4
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:43,961
[exhales]

5
00:00:47,339 --> 00:00:49,341
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

6
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:56,390
[crow cawing]

7
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:01,228
[host] Tuesday has begun.

8
00:01:11,405 --> 00:01:12,781
[ZZONE] This is driving me crazy.

9
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:17,286
ZZONE

10
00:01:17,369 --> 00:01:18,412
It's so strange.

11
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:20,163
Shit.

12
00:01:20,247 --> 00:01:22,249
ANOTHER HUNTER ON TUESDAY
SHIN JIEUN

13
00:01:22,833 --> 00:01:24,459
SHIN JIEUN

14
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:26,378
[Jieun] I think I'm screwed right now.

15
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:27,879
[panting softly]

16
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:30,173
I need to tag someone.

17
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:36,722
[panting]

18
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,435
[ZZONE] Where did they go?

19
00:01:43,687 --> 00:01:44,688
Where is everyone?

20
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:51,695
[ZZONE] I was so anxious and desperate
that I was panicking.

21
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:54,656
[panting, exhales]

22
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:56,825
You need to tag just anyone.

23
00:01:57,826 --> 00:02:00,537
All I could think about
was not coming in last,

24
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:03,540
so I came to the conclusion
that the only way I'd survive

25
00:02:03,623 --> 00:02:05,167
was by eliminating ZZONE.

26
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:07,627
So I went up to Joonsu

27
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:08,962
and just immediately said...

28
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:10,797
-Help.
-[Joonsu] What's wrong?

29
00:02:10,881 --> 00:02:13,050
JIEUN GOES TO HER ALLY JOONSU
WHO WAS HIDING

30
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,843
I need your help with tagging others.

31
00:02:14,926 --> 00:02:15,927
LEE JOONSU, SHIN JIEUN

32
00:02:17,888 --> 00:02:20,182
[Joonsu] We don't have much time.
What's your score?

33
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:22,351
[Jieun] I'm at minus 18.

34
00:02:22,434 --> 00:02:24,519
[Joonsu] Is there anyone else
with a lower score?

35
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:26,480
[Jieun] Can you give me two points?

36
00:02:26,563 --> 00:02:27,898
LOOKING AROUND

37
00:02:29,316 --> 00:02:31,568
-[Joonsu] Go ahead. Go ahead.
-If I end up...

38
00:02:31,652 --> 00:02:32,653
JIEUN TAGS JOONSU

39
00:02:32,736 --> 00:02:34,404
[host] Tag confirmed.

40
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:36,865
[Jieun] If I end up being eliminated,

41
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,075
-I won't pick you.
-[Joonsu] Okay.

42
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,159
SHIN JIEUN

43
00:02:39,242 --> 00:02:40,702
-Let's do that.
-[Jieun] Sorry.

44
00:02:40,786 --> 00:02:42,329
-[Joonsu] No worries.
-I had to beg you.

45
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:45,499
-[Joonsu] No, this is about being loyal.
-[Jieun] I'm sorry.

46
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:47,584
I wasn't at risk of getting eliminated.

47
00:02:47,668 --> 00:02:49,544
It's better to help her now

48
00:02:49,628 --> 00:02:53,090
so she can return the favor later
instead of refusing to help her.

49
00:02:53,173 --> 00:02:54,341
That was my strategy.

50
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:01,181
MEANWHILE, ZZONE HASN'T FOUND ANYONE

51
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:02,307
[ZZONE] This is insane.

52
00:03:10,357 --> 00:03:11,650
[sighs] This is driving me nuts.

53
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,402
-[alarm blaring]
-Gosh, that scared me.

54
00:03:13,485 --> 00:03:15,737
[host] Wednesday has begun.

55
00:03:15,821 --> 00:03:17,489
[ZZONE] I'm in trouble now.

56
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:22,828
I was a Wolf on Wednesday.

57
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:25,247
That day, there were five Wolves
and three Hunters.

58
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:26,790
There were way too many.

59
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:30,544
To avoid getting eliminated
without betraying anyone,

60
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:34,005
I figured the best thing to do
was hold out as long as possible.

61
00:03:34,089 --> 00:03:36,466
So, I stayed hidden
even while I was a Wolf.

62
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:39,302
[♪ tense music playing]

63
00:03:40,387 --> 00:03:42,848
I was trying to hold out anyway I could.

64
00:03:43,432 --> 00:03:45,600
MUYEONG FACTORY

65
00:03:45,684 --> 00:03:49,187
JANG EUNSIL

66
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:56,027
JANG EUNSIL HEADS TOWARD ZZONE

67
00:04:05,287 --> 00:04:07,539
[ZZONE whispering]
The footsteps sound so loud.

68
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:08,748
I'm losing my mind.

69
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:13,336
[footsteps approaching]

70
00:04:14,087 --> 00:04:16,006
[♪ sinister music playing]

71
00:04:20,135 --> 00:04:23,972
-[Eunsil] I put it on.
-I put it on. I tagged you.

72
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:27,058
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-[Eunsil] It's okay. My arm...

73
00:04:27,934 --> 00:04:30,228
-[ZZONE] I was so startled.
-Me too. [sighs]

74
00:04:30,312 --> 00:04:31,980
ZZONE AND EUNSIL TAG EACH OTHER

75
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:33,940
[ZZONE groans] I was so frustrated.

76
00:04:34,024 --> 00:04:37,152
If I held out a little longer,
it would have worked out.

77
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:39,571
I can't believe I got tagged there.

78
00:04:39,654 --> 00:04:41,156
I was so mad at myself.

79
00:04:41,865 --> 00:04:43,158
[host] Ms. ZZONE.

80
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:46,995
With a score of negative 23 points,
you've become an elimination candidate,

81
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,747
so please head to the Isolation Area.

82
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,373
[ZZONE] I guess Eunsil was a Hunter.

83
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:57,422
ZZONE HAS BEEN ISOLATED
FOR SCORING -20 POINTS OR LOWER

84
00:04:58,089 --> 00:05:01,468
When I saw that message,
I was glad it wasn't me.

85
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:03,512
I felt a little relieved.

86
00:05:04,429 --> 00:05:05,430
[sniffles]

87
00:05:08,892 --> 00:05:10,477
[woodchips rustling]

88
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:12,521
I'm dizzy.

89
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:14,439
[sighs]

90
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:21,404
I decided to keep my head down
and not draw attention to myself.

91
00:05:21,488 --> 00:05:23,740
I was going to lay low and wait it out.

92
00:05:23,824 --> 00:05:25,283
JIEUN MUST HOLD OUT SOMEHOW

93
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:30,372
[Horseking] I'm a Hunter on Wednesday.

94
00:05:31,498 --> 00:05:35,126
HORSEKING

95
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:36,211
[Horseking] In the second round,

96
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:39,881
I needed to stay in first place,

97
00:05:39,965 --> 00:05:42,968
so I figured I had to widen the gap
between me and the other players.

98
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:46,847
Also, I suspected Sanghyun was the Seeker,

99
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:49,933
and I didn't want him to get
the Elimination Immunity Pass.

100
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:52,227
That was my goal.

101
00:05:53,270 --> 00:05:55,564
YUK JUNSEO

102
00:05:55,647 --> 00:05:57,065
[Junseo] I was a Wolf on Wednesday.

103
00:05:57,148 --> 00:06:00,151
I did care about getting first place,

104
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:03,530
so I was very determined to catch people.

105
00:06:05,866 --> 00:06:06,867
[Horseking exhales]

106
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:08,994
Where are they?

107
00:06:09,077 --> 00:06:11,121
[groans] I need to tag people
while I'm a Hunter.

108
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:18,128
[sighs]

109
00:06:22,841 --> 00:06:23,884
[Horseking] Geez.

110
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:27,053
Finding someone
would be a miracle at that point

111
00:06:27,137 --> 00:06:29,806
because everyone was hiding,
so I couldn't see anyone.

112
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:32,267
They've all hidden so well.

113
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:36,146
As expected,
I knew everyone would be hiding.

114
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:39,190
But to me...

115
00:06:41,902 --> 00:06:44,487
Jaegyun!

116
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,197
Hey, Jaegyun!

117
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:50,869
Jaegyun was there.

118
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:54,289
-Jaegyun!
-[Jaegyun] Yeah?

119
00:06:54,372 --> 00:06:56,207
[Horseking] Help me.
I'll be in first if I tag someone.

120
00:06:56,291 --> 00:06:57,334
[Jaegyun] Then, I'll be minus 10...

121
00:06:57,417 --> 00:06:59,669
If you come in last place, I'll save you.

122
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:01,129
-Sure, go ahead.
-Thank you.

123
00:07:01,212 --> 00:07:02,213
HORSEKING TAGS JAEGYUN

124
00:07:02,297 --> 00:07:03,340
[host] Tag confirmed.

125
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:05,425
[Jaegyun] If I'm put up for elimination,
don't vote me out.

126
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:07,969
[Horseking] Of course not. Thank you.

127
00:07:08,053 --> 00:07:12,307
I realized politics would matter more
from that point on.

128
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:14,184
People may not know this,

129
00:07:15,101 --> 00:07:17,145
but I'm pretty good at politics.

130
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:20,649
I thought this could work
in my favor after all.

131
00:07:20,732 --> 00:07:21,733
LAST NIGHT
MEN'S QUARTERS

132
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:22,942
[Horseking] If...

133
00:07:23,026 --> 00:07:25,612
If you join our alliance, by any chance,

134
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:27,322
would we really need to fight each other?

135
00:07:27,405 --> 00:07:28,740
No, never.

136
00:07:28,823 --> 00:07:31,493
[Horseking] I mean, we don't want
to end up in last place.

137
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:33,119
HORSEKING JOINS FORCES WITH ROOMMATES

138
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:35,955
[Horseking] Joonsu!

139
00:07:37,749 --> 00:07:41,211
JOONSU WAS PART OF TWO SEPARATE ALLIANCES

140
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:43,296
[footsteps]

141
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:47,676
I need to tag three people now
to be in first place.

142
00:07:47,759 --> 00:07:49,594
But I'm at minus 7 points right now.

143
00:07:49,678 --> 00:07:51,346
Last place has already been decided.

144
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:54,099
-Then, that's settled?
-Yeah.

145
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:55,183
-Tag me.
-Okay, thank you.

146
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:56,267
HORSEKING TAGS JOONSU

147
00:07:56,351 --> 00:07:58,353
-Let's go. Get going.
-[host] Tag confirmed.

148
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:00,980
Thanks to Jaegyun and Joonsu,

149
00:08:01,064 --> 00:08:04,150
things went the way I wanted,
and I could play with ease.

150
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:06,528
I got four points
just by convincing people.

151
00:08:07,529 --> 00:08:08,863
On top of that...

152
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:12,492
There's someone over there.

153
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:15,662
[♪ foreboding music playing]

154
00:08:17,539 --> 00:08:18,540
[chuckles]

155
00:08:18,623 --> 00:08:20,041
I even found Jieun, who was hiding.

156
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:22,377
-Sorry?
-[Horseking] What's your score?

157
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:23,503
[Jieun] Me? 10...

158
00:08:24,254 --> 00:08:25,797
Earlier, I was tagged.

159
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,006
So, what's your score?

160
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:28,800
[Jieun] You're in first,
so why are you chasing?

161
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:29,884
-Why bother?
-You never know.

162
00:08:29,968 --> 00:08:33,304
I promise I'm going to stay here,
but if you really have to...

163
00:08:33,388 --> 00:08:36,057
If you have no choice later,
can't you come back then?

164
00:08:36,141 --> 00:08:38,560
I'm begging you, I promise I'll stay here.

165
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:40,770
-[chuckles]
-I swear, I'll stay right here.

166
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:42,939
Seriously, I'll keep hiding.

167
00:08:52,032 --> 00:08:53,158
Hold on.

168
00:08:56,286 --> 00:08:57,287
-Here.
-No, wait.

169
00:08:57,370 --> 00:08:58,371
HORSEKING TAGS JIEUN

170
00:08:58,455 --> 00:09:01,291
To be honest, I did hesitate for a moment,

171
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:03,877
but I had to win.

172
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,671
I guess I only focused on my own survival.

173
00:09:07,589 --> 00:09:09,257
[host] Tag confirmed.

174
00:09:25,190 --> 00:09:27,025
[♪ ominous music plays]

175
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:28,610
JANG EUNSIL APPEARS

176
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:30,153
[Eunsil] What are you?

177
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:31,237
Oh.

178
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:33,531
[exclaims]

179
00:09:34,115 --> 00:09:35,325
Oh.

180
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:38,244
[exclaims] Wait a minute.

181
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:40,080
[Eunsil] I got you.

182
00:09:40,747 --> 00:09:41,748
EUNSIL TAGS JUNSEO

183
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:43,333
[host] Tag confirmed.

184
00:09:44,667 --> 00:09:45,877
Are you a Hunter?

185
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:46,961
Yeah, I'm a Hunter.

186
00:09:47,045 --> 00:09:48,463
JANG EUNSIL

187
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:53,885
[Junseo] Eunsil charged at me
like a runaway train,

188
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:55,220
and I was totally stunned.

189
00:10:00,809 --> 00:10:05,146
-I'd like to check my score, please.
-[dealer] Sure, we will check your score.

190
00:10:05,230 --> 00:10:07,148
Your current score is two points.

191
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:10,276
YUK JUNSEO

192
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,361
[Junseo] Still,

193
00:10:11,444 --> 00:10:15,615
my rank wasn't as low as I'd feared,

194
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:16,866
so I was very relieved.

195
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:19,661
At that point,
I put my Wolf and Hunter marker

196
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,329
on Wednesday and Friday respectively.

197
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:23,456
I thought maybe I should tag

198
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:27,544
as many people as I could on Friday.

199
00:10:29,671 --> 00:10:31,506
Could you please check my placement?

200
00:10:31,589 --> 00:10:34,342
PLAYERS CAN CHECK THEIR MARKER PLACEMENT

201
00:10:34,926 --> 00:10:36,553
[dealer] You are a Wolf on Wednesday

202
00:10:37,679 --> 00:10:39,180
and a Hunter on Tuesday.

203
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:42,392
[♪ intriguing music playing]

204
00:10:45,687 --> 00:10:46,688
Okay.

205
00:10:47,814 --> 00:10:49,190
What is going on?

206
00:10:49,274 --> 00:10:51,734
I checked the placement chart again.

207
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:55,655
I saw that my Hunter marker
had been moved to Tuesday.

208
00:10:58,116 --> 00:11:00,326
[dealer] Mr. Yuk Junseo,
please place your marker

209
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:01,619
on the game board.

210
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:07,083
You have placed
your Hunter marker on Friday.

211
00:11:07,167 --> 00:11:08,168
Is this correct?

212
00:11:09,127 --> 00:11:10,879
[Junseo] I put my Hunter marker on Friday.

213
00:11:10,962 --> 00:11:12,505
For Wednesday and Friday,

214
00:11:12,589 --> 00:11:15,800
I'd worked out my plan
to secure points on each day.

215
00:11:15,884 --> 00:11:19,179
But when I saw the change,
my mind went blank for five seconds.

216
00:11:19,262 --> 00:11:23,641
All my plans fell apart
because my chance as a Hunter disappeared.

217
00:11:23,725 --> 00:11:28,146
I thought it might have
something to do with the Seeker's mission.

218
00:11:28,730 --> 00:11:30,190
Ah, I'm in trouble.

219
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:32,066
HORSEKING

220
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:34,736
YOUN SANGHYUN
YUK JUNSEO

221
00:11:40,491 --> 00:11:42,410
[Horseking] I'm exhausted. [sighs]

222
00:11:42,952 --> 00:11:43,953
[exhales]

223
00:11:44,454 --> 00:11:47,540
EUNSIL TAGGED JUNSEO

224
00:11:47,624 --> 00:11:48,958
Yuk Junseo was caught.

225
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:51,294
I thought, "This is my game."

226
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:53,129
I wanted to win my own game.

227
00:11:53,213 --> 00:11:54,380
IN FIRST WITH 11 POINTS

228
00:11:54,464 --> 00:11:57,008
I absolutely didn't want
to lose to Sanghyun.

229
00:11:57,091 --> 00:11:58,343
I had to win, no matter what.

230
00:11:58,426 --> 00:11:59,427
LOCKED IN

231
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:07,894
[alarm blaring]

232
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,938
[Sanghyun] Gosh, it's so cramped.

233
00:12:10,021 --> 00:12:11,356
ROUND 2 THURSDAY

234
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:12,482
What the heck?

235
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:16,819
-You... I'm a Hunter.
-What?

236
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:18,613
What are you?

237
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:21,574
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-I caught him.

238
00:12:21,658 --> 00:12:22,742
SANGHYUN TAGS HORSEKING

239
00:12:22,825 --> 00:12:25,036
Gosh, I almost lost it.

240
00:12:25,662 --> 00:12:28,498
All I had to do was stay hidden,
and I had it in the bag.

241
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:31,376
[hisses frustratedly]

242
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:35,964
But then, by incredible coincidence,

243
00:12:36,047 --> 00:12:37,924
Sanghyun came out

244
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:39,884
right next to me when he was a Wolf.

245
00:12:39,968 --> 00:12:42,428
-You... I'm a Hunter.
-What?

246
00:12:43,054 --> 00:12:44,681
[Horseking] Before I knew it,
he tagged me.

247
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:47,183
I was like, "What just happened?"
It felt a little off.

248
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:50,436
He didn't hesitate at all.

249
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:53,022
Whether it's this game or any other game,

250
00:12:53,106 --> 00:12:55,191
if you tag the wrong person,
you lose points,

251
00:12:55,275 --> 00:12:57,277
because the other person
could be a Hunter.

252
00:12:57,360 --> 00:13:00,363
So naturally,
you need to keep your guard up.

253
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:03,783
There's no way you can win
if you play like he did.

254
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:05,410
I was like, "What was that?"

255
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:07,912
Did he already know?

256
00:13:08,538 --> 00:13:09,914
-What?
-[Sanghyun] Wait, you're a Hunter?

257
00:13:09,998 --> 00:13:10,999
[Horseking] Yeah.

258
00:13:11,082 --> 00:13:12,750
[♪ intriguing music playing]

259
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:15,712
-[Sanghyun] Then, I'm screwed.
-[Horseking] That's right.

260
00:13:16,796 --> 00:13:18,840
-What can you do?
-I wondered why you stayed still.

261
00:13:18,923 --> 00:13:21,426
HORSEKING, YOUN SANGHYUN

262
00:13:21,509 --> 00:13:22,510
[Sanghyun] Sure.

263
00:13:23,553 --> 00:13:24,554
[patch rips]

264
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:27,015
-[dealer] Sanghyun has tagged Horseking.
-I'm so scared!

265
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:29,934
SANGHYUN RUNS AWAY AS SOON AS HE LEAVES

266
00:13:30,977 --> 00:13:32,854
[Horseking] Is he really the Seeker?

267
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:42,238
[panting]

268
00:13:44,115 --> 00:13:47,035
[dealer] Mr. Youn Sanghyun,
would you like to check your score?

269
00:13:48,703 --> 00:13:51,289
-Would you like to check your score?
-[Sanghyun] No, thank you.

270
00:13:52,331 --> 00:13:54,625
[♪ intriguing music intensifies]

271
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:57,670
Here.

272
00:14:10,933 --> 00:14:13,561
TUESDAY, WEDNESDAY,
THURSDAY, FRIDAY, SATURDAY

273
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:15,021
ZZONE, JIEUN, JIMIN

274
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,105
JOONSU, JUNSEO,
EUNSIL, HORSEKING

275
00:14:16,189 --> 00:14:17,732
SANGHYUN, JIMIN, EUNSIL

276
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:22,195
SANGHYUN CHECKS ALL THE MARKER PLACEMENTS

277
00:14:25,907 --> 00:14:29,494
THURSDAY
SANGHYUN, JIMIN, EUNSIL

278
00:14:30,286 --> 00:14:31,329
I knew.

279
00:14:35,208 --> 00:14:36,209
I got it.

280
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:37,293
30 MINUTES AGO

281
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:39,796
ROUND 2 TUESDAY

282
00:14:39,879 --> 00:14:41,839
[♪ mysterious music playing]

283
00:14:41,923 --> 00:14:45,802
The dealer in the Placement Room
was wearing contact lenses.

284
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:47,595
I was like, "Why would he do that?"

285
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:49,597
[Junseo] Do wolves usually have
different-colored eyes?

286
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,766
[Jaegyun] It's heterochromia.
Different colored eyes.

287
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:53,726
[Jimin] Don't you think
there are too many Wolves?

288
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:55,186
[Jaegyun] But there are only nine of us.

289
00:15:02,944 --> 00:15:04,403
[Sanghyun] He had a tag on him.

290
00:15:04,487 --> 00:15:07,490
He had a tag that the players have.

291
00:15:10,493 --> 00:15:11,577
So he's a Wolf.

292
00:15:11,661 --> 00:15:13,329
Could I see your back for a moment?

293
00:15:15,998 --> 00:15:17,458
[host] Tag confirmed.

294
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:19,460
[dealer] Mr. Youn Sanghyun.

295
00:15:19,544 --> 00:15:22,255
You have obtained a Marker Movement Pass.

296
00:15:31,848 --> 00:15:34,016
SANGHYUN, ZZONE, JIEUN

297
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:35,226
[gasps]

298
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:39,272
You may check
the marker placements of all players

299
00:15:39,355 --> 00:15:43,192
and move one of your markers
to a different time slot.

300
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:45,236
ZZONE, JOONSU, SANGHYUN

301
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:47,864
Except for Wednesday,
to place your marker on a day

302
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,949
that already has three markers,

303
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:52,910
you must push one marker out
before placing yours.

304
00:15:52,994 --> 00:15:54,453
Here is your marker

305
00:15:54,537 --> 00:15:57,290
to show you have obtained
the Marker Movement Pass.

306
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:03,129
HIDDEN MARKER
THE PLAYER WHO TAGS THE HIDDEN WOLF CAN

307
00:16:03,212 --> 00:16:05,131
VIEW MARKER PLACEMENTS OF ALL PLAYERS

308
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:06,883
MOVE ONE OF THEIR MARKERS ONCE

309
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:09,844
PUSH OUT A MARKER AND REASSIGN IT
IF CHOSEN DAY IS FULL

310
00:16:09,927 --> 00:16:12,180
[♪ intriguing music playing]

311
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:19,395
[Sanghyun] First, I placed a Hunter marker
on Friday, which had only one other Hunter

312
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:21,397
and pushed out Junseo's Hunter marker.

313
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:23,733
Tuesday.

314
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:29,906
I moved Junseo's Hunter marker to Tuesday
and pushed out my Wolf marker.

315
00:16:30,489 --> 00:16:32,783
Then, I pushed
Thursday's Hunter Joonsu out.

316
00:16:32,867 --> 00:16:35,995
Horseking wasn't on Thursday,
so I was the only one who could hunt.

317
00:16:36,078 --> 00:16:37,830
THURSDAY
EUNSIL, JIMIN, SANGHYUN

318
00:16:37,914 --> 00:16:42,043
Given how strong Horseking is physically,
I saw him as a threat.

319
00:16:42,126 --> 00:16:45,963
Since this game involves tagging people,

320
00:16:46,047 --> 00:16:50,009
I thought I couldn't win
through a battle of wits alone.

321
00:16:50,092 --> 00:16:51,093
PLACEMENT STATUS

322
00:16:51,177 --> 00:16:52,178
TUE, WED
SANGHYUN

323
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:53,262
FRI: SANGHYUN
TUE: JUNSEO

324
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:54,472
THU: SANGHYUN
SAT: JOONSU

325
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:56,599
THU, FRI
SANGHYUN

326
00:16:56,682 --> 00:16:58,351
-Thank you.
-[dealer] You're welcome.

327
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:06,651
SANGHYUN GOES LOOKING FOR A DOG

328
00:17:11,239 --> 00:17:12,949
[Sanghyun] I have to catch ZZONE.

329
00:17:13,532 --> 00:17:15,159
HWANG JAEGYUN

330
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,120
SANGHYUN GOES STRAIGHT TO JAEGYUN

331
00:17:18,204 --> 00:17:20,957
-[Jaegyun chuckles] Seriously... Come on.
-[Sanghyun laughs]

332
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:22,166
SANGHYUN TAGS JAEGYUN

333
00:17:22,250 --> 00:17:23,626
[host] Tag confirmed.

334
00:17:25,503 --> 00:17:27,171
[Jaegyun] Something's off.

335
00:17:27,255 --> 00:17:30,508
How did Sanghyun know that I was a Dog?

336
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:33,135
SANGHYUN TAGGED JAEGYUN

337
00:17:33,803 --> 00:17:35,805
[Horseking] So this is how the game
has turned out.

338
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:38,849
I'm a Wolf.

339
00:17:39,642 --> 00:17:40,893
-[alarm blaring]
-I can go in.

340
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:43,813
[host] Friday has begun.

341
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:45,523
[Horseking] To stay in first place,

342
00:17:46,107 --> 00:17:49,652
I had to tag everyone I could
when I was a Wolf.

343
00:17:50,361 --> 00:17:52,154
I thought I had to go for the win.

344
00:17:52,822 --> 00:17:56,284
[Sanghyun] It was pretty much a fight
between me and Horseking.

345
00:17:56,367 --> 00:17:59,620
I knew I had to take first place
so I wouldn't be voted as the Seeker.

346
00:18:02,123 --> 00:18:04,125
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

347
00:18:05,668 --> 00:18:07,086
I need to catch them.

348
00:18:11,382 --> 00:18:16,012
In Round 1, there were definitely
a lot of people around.

349
00:18:16,095 --> 00:18:18,222
But when Round 2 started, it got quiet.

350
00:18:18,306 --> 00:18:19,932
I didn't see anyone around.

351
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:22,435
ON THE OTHER HAND

352
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:24,020
[Horseking laughing]

353
00:18:31,193 --> 00:18:32,903
-[Eunsil] Oh, my gosh!
-What are you?

354
00:18:32,987 --> 00:18:34,030
1ST PLACE HORSEKING
8 POINTS

355
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:35,114
[host] Tag confirmed.

356
00:18:35,197 --> 00:18:36,824
1ST PLACE HORSEKING
11 POINTS

357
00:18:37,450 --> 00:18:40,161
2ND PLACE SANGHYUN
9 POINTS

358
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:41,287
Where are they?

359
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:42,830
HORSEKING'S LEAD ONCE AGAIN WIDENS

360
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:44,915
[panting]

361
00:18:46,751 --> 00:18:49,712
[Sanghyun] I was looking everywhere,
but I couldn't find a single person.

362
00:18:49,795 --> 00:18:54,300
But Horseking somehow kept finding people
and scoring points. I was amazed.

363
00:18:54,383 --> 00:18:56,510
How was Horseking
tagging all those people?

364
00:19:00,598 --> 00:19:01,599
[sighs]

365
00:19:01,682 --> 00:19:03,392
It was hard to find people.

366
00:19:19,575 --> 00:19:20,576
What are you?

367
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:23,537
[♪ tense music playing]

368
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:26,624
-[Junseo] What are you?
-Come on out first.

369
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:27,750
-[Junseo] What are you?
-What?

370
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:29,168
-[Junseo] What are you?
-I'm...

371
00:19:29,251 --> 00:19:31,671
-A Wolf.
-[Junseo] If you're a Wolf, just go away.

372
00:19:31,754 --> 00:19:33,631
-Why?
-[Junseo] There's no reason to fight.

373
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:35,591
-[Sanghyun] Why?
-Because I'm a Wolf.

374
00:19:35,675 --> 00:19:37,051
-What?
-[Junseo] Because I'm a Wolf.

375
00:19:37,718 --> 00:19:38,761
[exclaims]

376
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:41,347
[dealer] Yuk Junseo's Hunter marker.

377
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:42,848
Where would you like to move it?

378
00:19:42,932 --> 00:19:43,933
Tuesday.

379
00:19:45,476 --> 00:19:46,727
SANGHYUN KNOWS JUNSEO'S ROLE

380
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:48,437
-Junseo.
-[Junseo] You want to fight?

381
00:19:48,521 --> 00:19:49,939
[panting]

382
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:51,982
SANGHYUN TAGS JUNSEO

383
00:19:52,066 --> 00:19:53,943
[host] Tag confirmed.

384
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:56,362
[Junseo] How could you do that?

385
00:19:56,445 --> 00:19:58,030
HORSEKING, SANGHYUN TIED

386
00:19:58,698 --> 00:19:59,699
SANGHYUN COMES BACK WITH A TAG

387
00:19:59,782 --> 00:20:01,075
[Sanghyun] Horseking's busy finding

388
00:20:01,158 --> 00:20:02,827
-and catching people right now.
-[Junseo] I know.

389
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:07,790
ROUND 2 CURRENT RANKINGS
HORSEKING, SANGHYUN TIED FOR FIRST

390
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:09,542
[alarm blaring]

391
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:11,544
[host] Saturday has begun.

392
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:16,215
-[Sanghyun] I need to win anyway.
-Who are the Wolves?

393
00:20:16,966 --> 00:20:18,175
Who are the other ones?

394
00:20:18,801 --> 00:20:20,469
I don't know. I'm not sure about that.

395
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:22,221
How did you know I wasn't a Wolf then?

396
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:24,223
You just looked scared.

397
00:20:24,306 --> 00:20:25,891
-What?
-You looked scared.

398
00:20:27,435 --> 00:20:29,395
[Junseo] On what days were you a Hunter?

399
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:32,356
-[Sanghyun] I'll explain later.
-How?

400
00:20:33,566 --> 00:20:35,234
[Sanghyun] I can't tell you right now.

401
00:20:35,317 --> 00:20:36,902
[Junseo] Don't make
the explanation confusing.

402
00:20:36,986 --> 00:20:39,155
If you confuse me,
I'll accuse you of being the Seeker.

403
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:41,282
Well, I can't tell you right now.

404
00:20:41,365 --> 00:20:44,326
Why not? It's just us. Why can't you talk?

405
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:46,203
-The game's not over.
-Don't try to confuse me.

406
00:20:46,287 --> 00:20:47,913
-The game isn't over yet.
-Huh?

407
00:20:47,997 --> 00:20:50,958
[Sanghyun] Junseo suddenly went,
"You're the Seeker, right? Explain."

408
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:53,586
Then, he started to get angry at me.

409
00:20:53,669 --> 00:20:55,129
The game is almost over now.

410
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,213
[Sanghyun exhales]

411
00:20:57,840 --> 00:20:59,800
There's nothing I can do anyway.

412
00:20:59,884 --> 00:21:01,969
[Sanghyun] But I couldn't tell him
anything either.

413
00:21:06,891 --> 00:21:07,892
[sighs]

414
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,685
Horseking is way too fast.

415
00:21:10,895 --> 00:21:11,896
YUK JUNSEO

416
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:14,190
[Junseo] Sanghyun's
been giving off this vibe

417
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:16,150
that makes him seem really suspicious.

418
00:21:16,233 --> 00:21:18,944
I figured he had to be the Seeker.

419
00:21:19,028 --> 00:21:21,405
If the Seeker ends up
claiming first place too,

420
00:21:21,489 --> 00:21:23,908
it'll put everyone else at huge risk too.

421
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:29,538
[Sanghyun] Hold on! [laughing]

422
00:21:43,177 --> 00:21:45,179
[Sanghyun panting]

423
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:50,267
SANGHYUN RUNS AWAY
TO THE PLACEMENT ROOM

424
00:21:57,274 --> 00:22:00,361
Even Junseo,
the one person I thought I could trust,

425
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:02,488
began to suspect me.

426
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:04,907
I had no one to turn to.

427
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:07,827
RULE: CANNOT STAY IN PLACEMENT ROOM
FOR OVER TWO MINUTES

428
00:22:07,910 --> 00:22:10,663
[panting]

429
00:22:15,918 --> 00:22:17,127
[exhales]

430
00:22:21,966 --> 00:22:22,967
What?

431
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:25,511
-[grunts]
-[host] Tag confirmed.

432
00:22:25,594 --> 00:22:27,471
SANGHYUN AND JUNSEO TAG EACH OTHER

433
00:22:27,555 --> 00:22:28,848
It was at the same time.

434
00:22:28,931 --> 00:22:30,933
[both panting]

435
00:22:32,309 --> 00:22:33,727
-We can't do this.
-[Junseo] What?

436
00:22:33,811 --> 00:22:34,937
We can't do this.

437
00:22:36,856 --> 00:22:37,857
[sighs]

438
00:22:38,357 --> 00:22:40,776
I thought there was no way
I could let Horseking win

439
00:22:40,860 --> 00:22:42,278
for being more athletic.

440
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:46,907
Even though he played football,
I decided I had to catch him.

441
00:22:46,991 --> 00:22:48,617
I had to face him head-on.

442
00:22:50,953 --> 00:22:52,830
-Horseking.
-Are you going to tag me?

443
00:22:53,581 --> 00:22:55,583
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

444
00:23:10,723 --> 00:23:12,308
-[grunts]
-[Sanghyun laughs]

445
00:23:16,896 --> 00:23:20,357
HORSEKING BARELY GETS AWAY

446
00:23:24,528 --> 00:23:25,571
He's gone.

447
00:23:27,781 --> 00:23:30,618
HORSEKING'S INCREDIBLE ATHLETIC ABILITY

448
00:23:30,701 --> 00:23:32,494
[Sanghyun] He's so good.

449
00:23:32,578 --> 00:23:33,787
[exhales]

450
00:23:34,705 --> 00:23:37,374
If he wins simply
because of his physical abilities...

451
00:23:38,042 --> 00:23:39,043
[sighs frustratedly]

452
00:23:40,169 --> 00:23:42,421
I decided to do everything I could.

453
00:23:43,714 --> 00:23:46,926
[panting] Where... where are we now?

454
00:23:48,761 --> 00:23:52,139
[Horseking] Even when I was
running out of breath, I gave it my all.

455
00:23:52,222 --> 00:23:54,516
I didn't want to lose to Sanghyun.

456
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:56,518
He was the prime Seeker suspect,

457
00:23:56,602 --> 00:23:58,687
so I can't let him get
the Elimination Immunity Pass.

458
00:24:00,356 --> 00:24:03,442
[Sanghyun] Seriously, please. Please.

459
00:24:08,614 --> 00:24:10,491
[alarm blaring]

460
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:15,037
[host] "Time Between Dogs and Wolves"
has ended.

461
00:24:17,498 --> 00:24:18,791
[mic feedback]

462
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:21,418
Please gather in the Main Hall.

463
00:24:21,502 --> 00:24:24,630
We will announce
the results of the Main Match.

464
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:28,342
[Horseking] If my math is right,
I should be in first place.

465
00:24:30,010 --> 00:24:31,804
[Sanghyun] Please.

466
00:24:31,887 --> 00:24:33,722
I wanted to come in first.

467
00:24:35,683 --> 00:24:37,643
[host] In today's Main Match,

468
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:41,355
"Time Between Dogs and Wolves,"
the winner is...

469
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,902
Youn Sanghyun.

470
00:24:46,986 --> 00:24:48,445
-[Jaegyun gasps in awe]
-[Joonsu] What?

471
00:24:48,529 --> 00:24:50,531
-That's incredible.
-[Joonsu exclaims]

472
00:24:50,614 --> 00:24:52,992
[players applauding]

473
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:59,790
Geez, I thought
I was in a tie for first place.

474
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:02,626
[hisses frustratedly]
Is this how things ended up?

475
00:25:02,710 --> 00:25:04,336
[Sanghyun] I would've been
in serious danger

476
00:25:04,420 --> 00:25:05,754
without the Marker Movement Pass.

477
00:25:05,838 --> 00:25:09,049
If I were to say how much that pass
contributed to my win,

478
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:11,510
I'd say it was 100%.

479
00:25:11,593 --> 00:25:13,804
WHEN HE USED THE HIDDEN PASS

480
00:25:13,887 --> 00:25:17,474
I pushed out Junseo's marker.

481
00:25:17,558 --> 00:25:19,143
[inaudible dialogue]

482
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:22,104
And then, with my Wolf marker
that was pushed out,

483
00:25:22,187 --> 00:25:24,565
I pushed out Joonsu's Hunter marker
on Thursday

484
00:25:24,648 --> 00:25:26,358
and put my Wolf marker on Thursday.

485
00:25:27,735 --> 00:25:29,695
-[dealer] Where would you like to move it?
-To Saturday.

486
00:25:29,778 --> 00:25:32,197
After being pushed out,
Joonsu's marker was left.

487
00:25:32,281 --> 00:25:33,449
But I didn't want to waste it.

488
00:25:33,532 --> 00:25:37,119
I thought about where I could place it
to give me an advantage.

489
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,496
[breathes deeply]

490
00:25:41,790 --> 00:25:43,083
-That Hunter...
-[dealer] Yes?

491
00:25:43,167 --> 00:25:45,961
[Sanghyun] Yeah, if I place
Joonsu's marker on Friday,

492
00:25:46,045 --> 00:25:48,714
I can push out my own Hunter marker again.

493
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:50,632
[dealer] You can move it
from Friday to Saturday.

494
00:25:50,716 --> 00:25:53,302
-[Sanghyun] I'll do that.
-[dealer] All right.

495
00:25:54,178 --> 00:25:55,971
-Would you like to confirm this?
-Yes.

496
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:57,056
[dealer] All right, then.

497
00:25:57,139 --> 00:25:59,933
Mr. Youn Sanghyun,
your Hunter marker has moved to Saturday.

498
00:26:00,017 --> 00:26:01,602
-[Sanghyun] Thank you.
-Of course.

499
00:26:02,311 --> 00:26:03,312
CAN ONLY MOVE YOUR OWN MARKER

500
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:04,396
TUE, WED
SANGHYUN

501
00:26:04,480 --> 00:26:05,481
FRI: SANGHYUN
TUE: JUNSEO

502
00:26:05,564 --> 00:26:07,941
TAKING ADVANTAGE
OF DAILY THREE-PLAYER LIMIT

503
00:26:08,025 --> 00:26:09,026
THU, SAT
SANGHYUN

504
00:26:09,109 --> 00:26:12,196
SANGHYUN PULLED OFF
HIS DESIRED MARKER PLACEMENTS

505
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:14,698
[♪ rock music playing]

506
00:26:14,782 --> 00:26:17,993
RESULTS

507
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:23,165
[Sanghyun panting]

508
00:26:27,377 --> 00:26:30,631
[Sanghyun] At that moment,
Junseo was waiting out front.

509
00:26:30,714 --> 00:26:33,425
I thought, "This is actually good."

510
00:26:34,009 --> 00:26:36,136
Because I moved
my Hunter marker to Saturday.

511
00:26:36,220 --> 00:26:37,221
YUK JUNSEO, YOUN SANGHYUN

512
00:26:38,847 --> 00:26:41,141
-[grunts]
-[host] Tag confirmed.

513
00:26:41,225 --> 00:26:42,309
YOUN SANGHYUN, YUK JUNSEO

514
00:26:42,392 --> 00:26:43,769
HORSEKING, SANGHYUN TIED

515
00:26:43,852 --> 00:26:47,689
1ST SANGHYUN
2ND HORSEKING

516
00:26:47,773 --> 00:26:49,817
[dealer] Mr. Youn Sanghyun,
congratulations.

517
00:26:49,900 --> 00:26:52,486
Here is your 20 million won
and Elimination Immunity Pass.

518
00:26:52,569 --> 00:26:55,364
-Your funds will be kept in your locker.
-Okay.

519
00:26:55,447 --> 00:26:57,574
-[dealer] Please return to the Main Hall.
-Thank you.

520
00:26:57,658 --> 00:26:58,659
[Jimin groans]

521
00:26:58,742 --> 00:27:00,744
[players laughing]

522
00:27:02,121 --> 00:27:05,874
I guess he must have received
more of the Wolf's perks.

523
00:27:05,958 --> 00:27:07,000
Oh...

524
00:27:07,084 --> 00:27:08,836
But in the end...

525
00:27:08,919 --> 00:27:12,965
I have no idea.
I need them to explain what happened.

526
00:27:14,216 --> 00:27:15,717
He said he knew the rules.

527
00:27:15,801 --> 00:27:18,512
-Sanghyun knew.
-[Jimin] You knew the rules? Tell me.

528
00:27:20,681 --> 00:27:21,682
So...

529
00:27:22,266 --> 00:27:23,517
Well...

530
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:27,145
I looked around the Dealer Room carefully.

531
00:27:27,229 --> 00:27:29,857
-Why am I stuttering?
-No, go ahead.

532
00:27:29,940 --> 00:27:31,525
[Sanghyun] The dealer

533
00:27:31,608 --> 00:27:33,569
-was wearing contact lenses.
-[exclaims]

534
00:27:33,652 --> 00:27:35,571
[Sanghyun] That seemed a little strange.

535
00:27:35,654 --> 00:27:37,114
So I checked his back,

536
00:27:37,197 --> 00:27:40,075
and he had the same spot
for patches as we did.

537
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:41,243
[gasps]

538
00:27:41,326 --> 00:27:42,452
A Wolf!

539
00:27:42,536 --> 00:27:44,329
So I thought, "He's a Wolf."

540
00:27:44,997 --> 00:27:46,164
Then...

541
00:27:46,248 --> 00:27:48,458
There was one extra Wolf all along,

542
00:27:48,542 --> 00:27:50,878
-because the dealer...
-He was that one Wolf.

543
00:27:50,961 --> 00:27:52,170
[gasps, chuckles]

544
00:27:52,254 --> 00:27:54,256
-[Jimin gasps] You're a genius.
-[gasps]

545
00:27:54,339 --> 00:27:55,549
[Jieun] That's unbelievable.

546
00:27:56,425 --> 00:27:58,427
I had no idea! How would I know? [groans]

547
00:27:58,510 --> 00:28:01,513
I even heard them talk about it
before going into the room,

548
00:28:01,597 --> 00:28:04,099
but I thought, "What different eyes?"

549
00:28:04,808 --> 00:28:08,061
How did he figure that out?
I still don't get it.

550
00:28:08,145 --> 00:28:12,024
I just thought the theme
of the dealer's outfit was a Wolf.

551
00:28:12,524 --> 00:28:13,859
Geez.

552
00:28:13,942 --> 00:28:17,696
I thought he was just in costume as a Wolf
for the game's theme.

553
00:28:17,779 --> 00:28:19,907
I didn't think beyond that.

554
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:23,035
I thought, "Okay, I see."
And I left it at that.

555
00:28:23,619 --> 00:28:25,245
Then, I stuck a patch on him.

556
00:28:25,329 --> 00:28:27,372
And I could see the marker placements

557
00:28:27,456 --> 00:28:29,750
of all the players.

558
00:28:29,833 --> 00:28:31,585
And I was allowed to change things.

559
00:28:31,668 --> 00:28:33,086
So that's why mine was changed.

560
00:28:33,170 --> 00:28:36,590
I could move my Wolf and Hunter markers.

561
00:28:37,299 --> 00:28:38,467
You're such a keen...

562
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:40,302
[Sanghyun] I asked him
if I could take a look.

563
00:28:40,385 --> 00:28:42,471
[Jimin] Even I have to think
that was a great move.

564
00:28:42,554 --> 00:28:44,723
I have to admit that was a brilliant move.

565
00:28:44,806 --> 00:28:48,060
Sanghyun is capable of pulling off
a great move like that.

566
00:28:48,143 --> 00:28:50,187
I thought it'd be great if I could team up

567
00:28:50,270 --> 00:28:52,731
with someone like him
in a future Main Match.

568
00:28:52,814 --> 00:28:54,149
That's what I was thinking.

569
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:55,275
ALWAYS THINKING ALLIANCES

570
00:28:55,359 --> 00:28:58,403
When we all went in to check,
I thought he was a Wolf.

571
00:28:58,487 --> 00:29:02,741
Ah, first off, I was amazed
by how he figured that out.

572
00:29:02,824 --> 00:29:06,244
I was really impressed
by his eye for detail.

573
00:29:06,328 --> 00:29:08,372
It was freaking awesome.

574
00:29:08,455 --> 00:29:09,831
It was so amazing.

575
00:29:09,915 --> 00:29:12,042
[gasps in awe]
That was an incredible idea.

576
00:29:12,125 --> 00:29:13,919
It seems the perks were incredible.

577
00:29:17,714 --> 00:29:19,341
That's the benefit of being the Seeker.

578
00:29:19,424 --> 00:29:22,052
-[Horseking] Sorry?
-Is that the benefit of being the Seeker?

579
00:29:22,135 --> 00:29:23,679
It doesn't make sense.

580
00:29:23,762 --> 00:29:26,348
That could've been the Seeker's perk.

581
00:29:26,848 --> 00:29:29,726
So I'm saying
they could make it look that way.

582
00:29:29,810 --> 00:29:32,521
-[Jaegyun] Right.
-It could've been their only move to make.

583
00:29:32,604 --> 00:29:34,439
In that case...

584
00:29:37,109 --> 00:29:39,861
if we look at it from various angles,

585
00:29:39,945 --> 00:29:42,280
that itself could be the advantage.

586
00:29:42,364 --> 00:29:44,366
[♪ intriguing music playing]

587
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:51,748
Here's what I think.

588
00:29:51,832 --> 00:29:54,835
The Seeker always has absolute power

589
00:29:54,918 --> 00:29:58,547
and they can decide whether they want
to finish first or second.

590
00:29:58,630 --> 00:29:59,923
If you look at it that way,

591
00:30:00,007 --> 00:30:01,508
"MARKER MOVEMENT PASS
IS SEEKER'S PERK?"

592
00:30:01,591 --> 00:30:04,845
what you're saying
might be the Seeker's perk.

593
00:30:07,889 --> 00:30:10,308
Here's what I think.

594
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:13,061
A lot of you already suspected me.

595
00:30:13,145 --> 00:30:15,272
I was honestly drawing a lot of suspicion.

596
00:30:15,355 --> 00:30:19,026
In that situation, I wouldn't have to come
in first place if I were the Seeker.

597
00:30:19,109 --> 00:30:20,110
Think about it.

598
00:30:20,193 --> 00:30:22,654
Why would I try so hard
to take first place?

599
00:30:22,738 --> 00:30:23,864
That's true.

600
00:30:23,947 --> 00:30:25,907
[♪ intriguing music swells]

601
00:30:29,202 --> 00:30:32,080
The players must have thought
that I was definitely the Seeker

602
00:30:32,164 --> 00:30:33,915
and it was the Seeker's perk.

603
00:30:33,999 --> 00:30:36,084
I guess that's what they suspected.

604
00:30:36,168 --> 00:30:37,544
[mic feedback]

605
00:30:37,627 --> 00:30:39,629
[host] We will reveal
the elimination candidate

606
00:30:39,713 --> 00:30:40,714
from today's Main Match.

607
00:30:40,797 --> 00:30:42,674
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

608
00:30:43,383 --> 00:30:45,927
The elimination candidate
from today's Main Match is...

609
00:30:46,428 --> 00:30:48,305
ZZONE.

610
00:30:51,975 --> 00:30:53,727
[ZZONE] I was bracing myself for it.

611
00:30:53,810 --> 00:30:55,729
I was in serious trouble
and started to think

612
00:30:55,812 --> 00:30:57,439
about who to pick as another candidate.

613
00:30:58,148 --> 00:31:00,692
[host] We will announce
another elimination candidate.

614
00:31:01,401 --> 00:31:03,403
[ZZONE] What? Who is it?

615
00:31:03,487 --> 00:31:05,322
ANOTHER ELIMINATION CANDIDATE?

616
00:31:05,405 --> 00:31:07,365
I wish I could turn back time.

617
00:31:07,449 --> 00:31:09,201
[ZZONE] That means I have a second chance.

618
00:31:09,284 --> 00:31:12,954
I was surely up for elimination,
but there might be a sliver of hope.

619
00:31:13,538 --> 00:31:15,624
[host] The other
elimination candidate is...

620
00:31:18,460 --> 00:31:21,004
Shin Jieun.

621
00:31:21,838 --> 00:31:22,839
[sighs softly]

622
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:26,051
[players gasp]

623
00:31:26,134 --> 00:31:27,469
[ZZONE] It was shocking.

624
00:31:27,552 --> 00:31:30,889
But I was so relieved.
I was on the verge of being eliminated,

625
00:31:30,972 --> 00:31:32,724
I saw this as a great opportunity.

626
00:31:33,391 --> 00:31:34,392
[gasps]

627
00:31:35,268 --> 00:31:37,646
I just had to hold out quietly
for 30 seconds.

628
00:31:37,729 --> 00:31:40,440
But during those 30 seconds,
I was shaking from fear.

629
00:31:43,777 --> 00:31:46,279
I kept hiding.

630
00:31:46,363 --> 00:31:48,323
After hiding for so long,

631
00:31:48,406 --> 00:31:50,492
I had a wake-up call.

632
00:31:50,575 --> 00:31:53,829
I realized I was hiding like a coward

633
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:56,957
and waiting for someone else
to get eliminated.

634
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:59,334
I realized that wasn't my style.

635
00:31:59,417 --> 00:32:03,046
So, I decided
to at least try to earn a point.

636
00:32:03,130 --> 00:32:04,339
And I did some thinking.

637
00:32:04,422 --> 00:32:08,135
It was Saturday, and Sanghyun was a Dog.

638
00:32:08,218 --> 00:32:10,262
I was 99% sure.

639
00:32:10,345 --> 00:32:12,139
I figured there was no way

640
00:32:12,222 --> 00:32:15,100
I'd end up being pushed
into the bottom of the rankings.

641
00:32:15,183 --> 00:32:18,812
So when I saw Sanghyun,
I rushed over and tagged him.

642
00:32:21,731 --> 00:32:22,774
[Sanghyun] Why are you chasing me?

643
00:32:24,609 --> 00:32:25,902
SANGHYUN & JIEUN TAG EACH OTHER

644
00:32:25,986 --> 00:32:26,987
Let's go.

645
00:32:27,612 --> 00:32:29,573
I got points out of this, so I was glad.

646
00:32:29,656 --> 00:32:31,324
So I tagged her at the same time.

647
00:32:31,408 --> 00:32:35,662
Also, her score went below -20
while I got points.

648
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:36,746
SHIN JIEUN

649
00:32:37,330 --> 00:32:39,291
[laughing]

650
00:32:40,083 --> 00:32:41,084
[groans]

651
00:32:41,877 --> 00:32:44,713
[host] ZZONE and Shin Jieun
are elimination candidates.

652
00:32:46,756 --> 00:32:48,717
[sighs] At the end, I shouldn't have...

653
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:50,802
[♪ tense music playing]

654
00:32:52,971 --> 00:32:55,056
[Joonsu] The three of us were a team.

655
00:32:55,140 --> 00:32:57,434
And the two of them
became elimination candidates.

656
00:32:57,517 --> 00:32:59,561
Ah, it was such a shame.

657
00:32:59,644 --> 00:33:01,479
But I didn't get picked.

658
00:33:02,314 --> 00:33:04,774
[host] Since there are
two elimination candidates,

659
00:33:04,858 --> 00:33:06,526
today's elimination candidate

660
00:33:06,610 --> 00:33:09,863
will be decided by the winner,
Youn Sanghyun.

661
00:33:09,946 --> 00:33:10,947
[sighs]

662
00:33:11,448 --> 00:33:12,908
-That's going to be hard.
-[host] Youn Sanghyun.

663
00:33:12,991 --> 00:33:15,202
-He'll be making an enemy.
-[host] Please go to the Dealer Room

664
00:33:15,785 --> 00:33:17,120
and choose one player

665
00:33:17,204 --> 00:33:21,166
between ZZONE and Shin Jieun.

666
00:33:22,417 --> 00:33:25,503
First place comes with insane power.

667
00:33:26,213 --> 00:33:29,049
You're not even going to give me
the chance to beg?

668
00:33:29,132 --> 00:33:31,635
I polished my knees to beg.

669
00:33:31,718 --> 00:33:33,220
[laughing]

670
00:33:34,221 --> 00:33:35,555
[Jieun] I was so sad.

671
00:33:35,639 --> 00:33:39,726
At the end, I shouldn't have messed
with Sanghyun, of all people.

672
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:43,438
[ZZONE] Sanghyun was looking at me.

673
00:33:43,521 --> 00:33:45,649
I felt like he'd pick me
if I looked cheerful.

674
00:33:45,732 --> 00:33:48,944
I was pretending to be helpless
so he'd feel sorry for me.

675
00:33:49,736 --> 00:33:50,820
What should I do...

676
00:33:52,280 --> 00:33:53,573
[Eunsil] Are you going right away?

677
00:33:56,660 --> 00:33:59,496
[dealer] Mr. Youn Sanghyun,
please choose the elimination candidate.

678
00:33:59,579 --> 00:34:01,957
SHIN JIEUN, ZZONE

679
00:34:09,631 --> 00:34:12,133
[host] The elimination candidate
has been selected.

680
00:34:13,093 --> 00:34:16,388
Between ZZONE and Shin Jieun,

681
00:34:16,471 --> 00:34:19,808
the elimination candidate selected
by winner Youn Sanghyun is...

682
00:34:21,351 --> 00:34:23,103
Shin Jieun.

683
00:34:23,853 --> 00:34:26,815
IN TIME BETWEEN DOGS AND WOLVES,
SHIN JIEUN HAS BEEN ELIMINATED

684
00:34:27,399 --> 00:34:29,609
[Sanghyun] I chose Shin Jieun
for elimination

685
00:34:30,610 --> 00:34:33,238
because she suspected me
of being the Seeker.

686
00:34:33,321 --> 00:34:35,490
I think Sanghyun is my number one suspect

687
00:34:35,573 --> 00:34:36,574
-as the Seeker.
-Yeah.

688
00:34:36,658 --> 00:34:37,993
Then, vote me out.

689
00:34:38,076 --> 00:34:39,953
-I'm testing you.
-How many times will you say it?

690
00:34:40,036 --> 00:34:41,830
Don't cry. Don't cry, don't cry.

691
00:34:41,913 --> 00:34:44,291
And Horseking tagged Jieun.

692
00:34:44,874 --> 00:34:46,876
-Here.
-No, wait.

693
00:34:46,960 --> 00:34:50,380
I heard from Horseking
that they'd made a certain deal.

694
00:34:50,463 --> 00:34:52,090
-You really need to help me.
-Me too.

695
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:53,466
I'll help you out later.

696
00:34:53,550 --> 00:34:55,051
Seriously!

697
00:34:55,135 --> 00:34:58,763
Anyhow, it was a battle
between me and Horseking.

698
00:34:58,847 --> 00:35:02,934
Since she helped him,
I felt like she'd turned against me.

699
00:35:04,019 --> 00:35:07,355
[Jieun] I knew he'd pick me.
I made him upset.

700
00:35:07,439 --> 00:35:10,317
[ZZONE groans]
I survived. It was such a relief.

701
00:35:11,443 --> 00:35:12,694
[host] Shin Jieun has been selected

702
00:35:12,777 --> 00:35:15,405
by Youn Sanghyun
as the elimination candidate

703
00:35:15,488 --> 00:35:17,866
and will now compete in the Death Match.

704
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:21,244
Please go to the Dealer Room
and pick two players besides Youn Sanghyun

705
00:35:21,328 --> 00:35:25,290
who will join you in the Death Match.

706
00:35:26,249 --> 00:35:27,250
[exhales heavily]

707
00:35:28,918 --> 00:35:31,212
[♪ mysterious music playing]

708
00:35:33,923 --> 00:35:35,342
-Ms. Shin Jieun.
-Yes?

709
00:35:35,425 --> 00:35:37,677
Please select two elimination candidates.

710
00:35:38,595 --> 00:35:39,638
[exhales heavily]

711
00:35:40,930 --> 00:35:42,724
I feel like she'll pick male players.

712
00:35:44,392 --> 00:35:46,102
There are two options.

713
00:35:46,811 --> 00:35:50,440
She'll either pick weaker ones
for the Death Match

714
00:35:50,523 --> 00:35:53,068
-or strong ones. It could be either way.
-Right.

715
00:35:53,151 --> 00:35:55,862
I think she'll choose me and Junseo.

716
00:35:56,988 --> 00:35:58,907
-I think it'll be me.
-[Joonsu] Why?

717
00:35:58,990 --> 00:35:59,991
Just a hunch.

718
00:36:01,326 --> 00:36:03,912
[Joonsu] ZZONE, Jieun, and I promised
we'd pick someone else

719
00:36:03,995 --> 00:36:06,456
even if we ended up coming in last.

720
00:36:06,539 --> 00:36:08,583
And no voting each other out.

721
00:36:08,667 --> 00:36:10,043
-[ZZONE] Sounds good.
-Promise.

722
00:36:10,126 --> 00:36:13,630
[Jieun] If I end up being eliminated,
I won't pick you.

723
00:36:14,464 --> 00:36:17,926
[Joonsu] I didn't think it'd be me,
so I felt relieved.

724
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:19,969
It's taking quite a while.

725
00:36:21,262 --> 00:36:22,263
[groans]

726
00:36:25,517 --> 00:36:26,518
[sighs]

727
00:36:31,523 --> 00:36:32,565
These two.

728
00:36:36,611 --> 00:36:38,613
HORSEKING, YUK JUNSEO

729
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:41,116
[mic feedback]

730
00:36:41,199 --> 00:36:43,952
[host] We will announce the results.

731
00:36:44,035 --> 00:36:47,580
The players Shin Jieun chose
as her Death Match opponents are...

732
00:36:49,165 --> 00:36:50,166
ZZONE

733
00:36:51,459 --> 00:36:53,169
and Lee Joonsu.

734
00:36:54,504 --> 00:36:55,755
[exclaims]

735
00:36:55,839 --> 00:36:57,257
But they teamed up for the game.

736
00:36:58,133 --> 00:36:59,676
-She picked them...
-That's unexpected.

737
00:36:59,759 --> 00:37:01,636
...to win the match.

738
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:03,680
[Joonsu sighs] Jieun...

739
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:06,891
My heart just fell.

740
00:37:06,975 --> 00:37:10,061
It felt worse than getting rejected
from college.

741
00:37:10,145 --> 00:37:12,188
Why would she betray me?

742
00:37:12,772 --> 00:37:15,316
[ZZONE] At that moment,
I was really annoyed.

743
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:16,443
[sighs frustratedly]

744
00:37:16,526 --> 00:37:19,863
So she just picked
the easiest opponents to beat right away

745
00:37:19,946 --> 00:37:21,489
in the Death Match.

746
00:37:23,616 --> 00:37:25,368
Am I being dumb?

747
00:37:26,077 --> 00:37:27,746
[groans] What a damn knucklehead.

748
00:37:28,705 --> 00:37:29,914
ZZONE...

749
00:37:30,707 --> 00:37:32,834
I actually want to pick these two,

750
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:34,753
but should I be selfish instead?

751
00:37:34,836 --> 00:37:37,130
But they were on my team.

752
00:37:37,213 --> 00:37:39,966
There were many moments
when I needed allies,

753
00:37:40,049 --> 00:37:44,429
so I thought I might need allies
in the Death Match too.

754
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:47,307
So I thought it might be advantageous

755
00:37:47,390 --> 00:37:50,351
to go with stronger players.

756
00:37:50,435 --> 00:37:52,437
That's why I was going to pick these two.

757
00:37:52,520 --> 00:37:53,605
HORSEKING, YUK JUNSEO

758
00:37:53,688 --> 00:37:55,732
But this is a gamble, after all.

759
00:37:55,815 --> 00:37:59,235
I kind of wanted to survive.

760
00:37:59,319 --> 00:38:00,320
[groans]

761
00:38:00,904 --> 00:38:01,946
I feel so guilty.

762
00:38:03,323 --> 00:38:07,994
I found myself wanting to be
a bit more safe and make sure I survive.

763
00:38:08,077 --> 00:38:09,913
I could team up with them,

764
00:38:09,996 --> 00:38:11,915
or if I went head-to-head with them,

765
00:38:11,998 --> 00:38:14,501
they were people I could beat.

766
00:38:14,584 --> 00:38:18,171
I thought I should choose people
who'd fit both of those criteria.

767
00:38:18,713 --> 00:38:21,132
[dealer] Your final choice
has been confirmed.

768
00:38:21,216 --> 00:38:22,217
[sighs] Okay.

769
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:24,010
DEATH MATCH CANDIDATES
ZZONE AND LEE JOONSU

770
00:38:25,637 --> 00:38:28,223
[Horseking] ZZONE and Joonsu
must be really stressed out.

771
00:38:28,306 --> 00:38:31,684
[host] We'll now begin the vote
between the two candidates,

772
00:38:31,768 --> 00:38:34,813
ZZONE and Lee Joonsu.

773
00:38:34,896 --> 00:38:36,856
VOTING BEGINS

774
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:41,110
Voting will close in an hour.

775
00:38:41,194 --> 00:38:44,989
-[Eunsil] Didn't you team up in the game?
-[ZZONE] We did. [chuckles]

776
00:38:45,073 --> 00:38:47,075
-[Eunsil] She betrayed you.
-[ZZONE laughs]

777
00:38:47,158 --> 00:38:49,702
-It's about survival.
-[Eunsil] That's true.

778
00:38:50,286 --> 00:38:53,414
[ZZONE] I guess the two of us
were too focused on our alliance.

779
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:56,000
[Joonsu] But why us?

780
00:38:56,084 --> 00:38:57,085
I don't get it.

781
00:38:57,669 --> 00:38:59,754
[ZZONE] Because we're the easiest ones
to beat.

782
00:38:59,838 --> 00:39:01,923
But we were a team.

783
00:39:02,966 --> 00:39:05,468
This is ridiculous.

784
00:39:06,511 --> 00:39:08,638
I genuinely trusted her.

785
00:39:09,347 --> 00:39:11,015
-Help me.
-Go ahead.

786
00:39:11,099 --> 00:39:13,268
[Joonsu] I let her tag me.

787
00:39:13,893 --> 00:39:17,105
I even let her tag me on purpose
so she could get points.

788
00:39:17,188 --> 00:39:18,356
Right.

789
00:39:18,439 --> 00:39:20,149
[Joonsu] I even let her tag me.

790
00:39:20,233 --> 00:39:21,234
[chuckles softly]

791
00:39:22,360 --> 00:39:23,945
She was once our teammate,

792
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:27,156
so I don't want to ask her
for a favor with money.

793
00:39:27,240 --> 00:39:28,449
I'll let them handle it.

794
00:39:28,992 --> 00:39:30,410
I'll let them take care of it.

795
00:39:30,910 --> 00:39:33,204
[Joonsu] Had it been someone else
and not ZZONE,

796
00:39:33,288 --> 00:39:35,498
I would've offered 10 million won

797
00:39:36,457 --> 00:39:40,336
and begged them not to pick me.

798
00:39:40,420 --> 00:39:42,463
But ZZONE was on my team.

799
00:39:43,214 --> 00:39:45,800
So I just figured
they'd pick the right person.

800
00:39:47,886 --> 00:39:51,180
[dealer] Mr. Lee Joonsu,
please cast your vote for elimination.

801
00:39:51,931 --> 00:39:53,558
[Joonsu] So I just voted for ZZONE

802
00:39:53,641 --> 00:39:54,684
"JOONSU VOTED FOR ZZONE"

803
00:39:54,767 --> 00:39:56,519
and decided to accept the results.

804
00:39:59,397 --> 00:40:00,773
[exhales]

805
00:40:00,857 --> 00:40:03,610
-[Joonsu] Are you crying? Why?
-Geez.

806
00:40:04,485 --> 00:40:06,404
[chuckles, sniffles]

807
00:40:07,822 --> 00:40:09,741
If I... [chuckles]

808
00:40:09,824 --> 00:40:11,200
If I did well in the game,

809
00:40:11,284 --> 00:40:13,745
-I would've spoken up.
-[Joonsu] You did well. We were a team.

810
00:40:13,828 --> 00:40:14,829
Not really.

811
00:40:16,748 --> 00:40:18,082
I was terrible.

812
00:40:18,166 --> 00:40:20,668
[ZZONE] First, I was so upset
that I got betrayed.

813
00:40:20,752 --> 00:40:24,672
On top of that, it was frustrating to lose
and become an elimination candidate.

814
00:40:24,756 --> 00:40:27,300
All those emotions piled up
and came out as tears.

815
00:40:32,347 --> 00:40:36,392
JOONSU IS AWAY FROM THE GROUP
AND KEEPS TO HIMSELF

816
00:40:38,019 --> 00:40:41,606
[Horseking] Joonsu
is normally super social.

817
00:40:42,941 --> 00:40:45,568
You have to help me this time.
Please help me.

818
00:40:45,652 --> 00:40:47,487
JOONSU ACTIVELY WENT AROUND DURING VOTING

819
00:40:47,570 --> 00:40:48,905
Please help me out just this once.

820
00:40:49,489 --> 00:40:52,951
JOONSU IS UNUSUALLY QUIET THIS TIME

821
00:40:53,534 --> 00:40:55,578
I really have no clue. What do I do?

822
00:40:55,662 --> 00:40:57,622
The Seeker exists in this game.

823
00:40:57,705 --> 00:41:01,000
I'm not sure if we should pick the person
we suspect is the Seeker.

824
00:41:01,793 --> 00:41:04,128
[Jaegyun] What should we do?
Who should I pick?

825
00:41:04,212 --> 00:41:07,382
If this is the case, let's have everyone
follow their instincts.

826
00:41:10,218 --> 00:41:13,388
ELIMINATION CANDIDATE VOTE

827
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:14,472
LEE JOONSU

828
00:41:14,555 --> 00:41:16,808
Joonsu would tell me

829
00:41:16,891 --> 00:41:18,393
one thing,

830
00:41:18,476 --> 00:41:20,353
but then act differently.

831
00:41:20,436 --> 00:41:22,271
[Jaegyun] Hey, Joonsu tagged me twice.

832
00:41:22,355 --> 00:41:23,356
IN ROUND 1

833
00:41:23,856 --> 00:41:26,609
JOONSU ACTED LIKE HE TAGGED HIM
AND RAN AWAY

834
00:41:26,693 --> 00:41:27,944
Where did he go?

835
00:41:28,528 --> 00:41:31,489
So, we know one person will be ZZONE.

836
00:41:31,572 --> 00:41:34,951
PROMISED TO VOTE OUT ZZONE WITH DAIL

837
00:41:36,452 --> 00:41:38,037
ELIMINATION CANDIDATE VOTE
YANG DAIL

838
00:41:38,121 --> 00:41:39,497
JOONSU VOTED FOR YANG DAIL

839
00:41:39,580 --> 00:41:43,751
[Jaegyun] I thought he could become
a potential threat to me.

840
00:41:45,253 --> 00:41:46,462
ELIMINATION CANDIDATE VOTE

841
00:41:46,546 --> 00:41:47,839
[Horseking] I voted for ZZONE.

842
00:41:47,922 --> 00:41:50,883
Joonsu is someone
who can cover my weak points.

843
00:41:50,967 --> 00:41:54,387
He's able to move around
between different sides.

844
00:41:54,470 --> 00:41:56,472
He keeps me updated on what he hears.

845
00:41:56,556 --> 00:41:58,307
I think he's a really good partner.

846
00:41:59,017 --> 00:42:00,059
[sighs]

847
00:42:00,143 --> 00:42:03,396
[Jimin] I was really torn,
because I really like both.

848
00:42:03,479 --> 00:42:06,357
It's partly because
they're such good listeners.

849
00:42:06,441 --> 00:42:07,483
BEFORE SEEKER VOTE YESTERDAY

850
00:42:07,567 --> 00:42:10,236
Horseking was able
to talk his way through it at the end,

851
00:42:10,319 --> 00:42:11,863
and Pani Bottle fell for it.

852
00:42:11,946 --> 00:42:13,948
I realized yesterday he was so persuasive.

853
00:42:14,032 --> 00:42:15,366
ZZONE SUPPORTED JIMIN'S OPINION

854
00:42:15,450 --> 00:42:18,161
-I wouldn't notice if he lied.
-I want to ask Joonsu this.

855
00:42:18,244 --> 00:42:20,538
Do you still trust him?

856
00:42:20,621 --> 00:42:22,331
I believed him up until now.

857
00:42:22,415 --> 00:42:23,875
You don't suspect him as the Seeker?

858
00:42:23,958 --> 00:42:26,002
I didn't, but I kind of do now.

859
00:42:26,085 --> 00:42:27,253
-[Jimin] Come on!
-[players laugh]

860
00:42:27,336 --> 00:42:28,337
GULLIBLE JOONSU

861
00:42:28,421 --> 00:42:31,591
I have a lot to gain from these two,
so I don't want to lose them.

862
00:42:31,674 --> 00:42:34,802
I'd rather take out someone
like Horseking, to be honest.

863
00:42:34,886 --> 00:42:38,473
Wouldn't it be better to choose someone
who can come back then?

864
00:42:39,057 --> 00:42:40,975
ELIMINATION CANDIDATE VOTE

865
00:42:41,059 --> 00:42:42,477
JIMIN VOTED FOR JOONSU

866
00:42:43,061 --> 00:42:46,647
I thought he'd do better and win,
so that's why I picked him.

867
00:42:47,523 --> 00:42:49,108
[dealer] Ms. Jang Eunsil.

868
00:42:49,609 --> 00:42:51,027
ELIMINATION CANDIDATE VOTE

869
00:42:51,110 --> 00:42:52,361
JANG EUNSIL VOTED FOR JOONSU

870
00:42:52,445 --> 00:42:55,823
[Eunsil] I was hoping
Joonsu would come back

871
00:42:55,907 --> 00:42:57,366
after winning the Death Match

872
00:42:57,450 --> 00:42:59,202
since he's the stronger player.

873
00:42:59,285 --> 00:43:01,287
LEE JOONSU, 3 VOTES
JAEGYUN, EUNSIL, JIMIN

874
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:03,206
ZZONE, 2 VOTES
JOONSU, HORSEKING

875
00:43:04,040 --> 00:43:05,041
-[dealer] Ms. ZZONE.
-Yes.

876
00:43:05,124 --> 00:43:07,251
[dealer] Please vote
for the player to be eliminated.

877
00:43:11,547 --> 00:43:13,800
ELIMINATION CANDIDATE VOTE
ZZONE

878
00:43:14,383 --> 00:43:15,802
I didn't like how the prison players

879
00:43:15,885 --> 00:43:18,429
had been seeing me
as an easy target since yesterday.

880
00:43:18,513 --> 00:43:20,973
It's so annoying

881
00:43:21,057 --> 00:43:23,351
that they thought I was the weakest one.

882
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:26,104
I wanted to return with my head held high
and prove myself.

883
00:43:26,187 --> 00:43:27,939
I'll vote for myself.

884
00:43:29,315 --> 00:43:31,275
LEE JOONSU, 3 VOTES
JAEGYUN, EUNSIL, JIMIN

885
00:43:31,359 --> 00:43:33,236
ZZONE, 3 VOTES
JOONSU, HORSEKING, ZZONE

886
00:43:33,861 --> 00:43:35,696
[host] We will announce the results.

887
00:43:37,156 --> 00:43:39,992
The player who will be sent directly
to the Death Match is...

888
00:43:42,578 --> 00:43:44,455
Lee Joonsu.

889
00:43:46,582 --> 00:43:47,583
[ZZONE] What?

890
00:43:49,544 --> 00:43:51,796
[Joonsu] I just felt upset.

891
00:43:53,923 --> 00:43:55,925
[♪ rock music playing]

892
00:43:57,552 --> 00:43:59,303
I don't know who to pick.

893
00:43:59,387 --> 00:44:00,388
I have no idea.

894
00:44:00,471 --> 00:44:02,932
-We should vote for Joonsu.
-[Sanghyun] Are you suspicious of him?

895
00:44:03,015 --> 00:44:04,976
[Junseo] In every game,

896
00:44:05,059 --> 00:44:07,311
I can't tell
if he's just naturally curious

897
00:44:07,395 --> 00:44:11,732
or if he's intentionally
trying to stir things up.

898
00:44:11,816 --> 00:44:15,111
I can't figure it out yet,
but it definitely bothers me.

899
00:44:15,194 --> 00:44:16,404
JOONSU'S PLAY RAISED SUSPICIONS

900
00:44:16,487 --> 00:44:18,322
That's why.

901
00:44:19,532 --> 00:44:20,825
I think that makes sense.

902
00:44:23,369 --> 00:44:24,412
[host] Lee Joonsu,

903
00:44:24,495 --> 00:44:28,166
please leave the area immediately
and get ready for the Death Match.

904
00:44:31,294 --> 00:44:32,712
I'll come back in one piece.

905
00:44:34,297 --> 00:44:35,548
See you later.

906
00:44:37,383 --> 00:44:40,428
[Joonsu] I will pull this off
and come back.

907
00:44:40,511 --> 00:44:41,554
I'll win, no matter what.

908
00:44:41,637 --> 00:44:44,849
People see me as the underdog,

909
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:47,059
and people are more likely
to feel sorry for me.

910
00:44:47,143 --> 00:44:50,605
I'm starting to think,
"Maybe this isn't a bad thing."

911
00:44:51,814 --> 00:44:52,815
[bell dings]

912
00:44:53,316 --> 00:44:55,276
[Pani Bottle]
The Death Match is beginning.

913
00:44:56,694 --> 00:45:00,072
We might end up going home today.
So let's look good until the end.

914
00:45:00,156 --> 00:45:01,157
[laughs]

915
00:45:01,282 --> 00:45:03,743
I got myself into the Death Match
like a God damn idiot.

916
00:45:03,826 --> 00:45:06,829
Making stupid mistakes again
and getting eliminated is...

917
00:45:07,788 --> 00:45:10,875
[exhales] ...something
I don't even want to imagine.

918
00:45:10,958 --> 00:45:13,085
I don't care who gets taken out.
I need to survive.

919
00:45:13,711 --> 00:45:15,338
[Sujin] I was put in prison from day one.

920
00:45:15,421 --> 00:45:17,423
After staying in prison for a while,

921
00:45:17,506 --> 00:45:18,799
I've had enough.

922
00:45:18,883 --> 00:45:20,593
I need to survive this.

923
00:45:20,676 --> 00:45:22,386
[Dail] We have to survive somehow.

924
00:45:23,304 --> 00:45:25,431
At the end of the day,
it's all about the results.

925
00:45:26,057 --> 00:45:28,684
I need to find out who the Seeker is.

926
00:45:29,894 --> 00:45:33,564
We were committed to coming back
and catching the Seeker.

927
00:45:33,648 --> 00:45:35,650
To the two people
coming to the Death Match,

928
00:45:35,733 --> 00:45:38,152
I'm sorry,
but you'll need to go home first.

929
00:45:39,445 --> 00:45:40,446
That's what I think.

930
00:45:41,072 --> 00:45:43,824
MUYEONG MARKET

931
00:45:44,408 --> 00:45:45,701
[Pani Bottle sighs]

932
00:45:48,579 --> 00:45:51,374
[Ddolddol gasps]
It's like a haunted house.

933
00:45:51,958 --> 00:45:53,292
[Sujin] I feel
an intense rush of dopamine.

934
00:45:54,377 --> 00:45:55,378
I'm going to survive.

935
00:45:56,254 --> 00:45:58,506
[Dail] Are we using
this entire outdoor area?

936
00:45:59,006 --> 00:46:00,341
[Sujin] It's bigger than I thought.

937
00:46:00,424 --> 00:46:01,759
[Dail] It's going to be exhausting.

938
00:46:11,143 --> 00:46:12,603
Someone's waiting over there.

939
00:46:12,687 --> 00:46:14,355
-It's Yuk Junseo.
-Who's that?

940
00:46:15,231 --> 00:46:16,524
Hello.

941
00:46:17,608 --> 00:46:18,609
Who is it?

942
00:46:21,195 --> 00:46:22,488
It's not Yuk Junseo.

943
00:46:23,072 --> 00:46:24,824
[Dail] I didn't know Joonsu
would be there.

944
00:46:24,907 --> 00:46:28,035
But as for me,
I'm not intimidated by anyone.

945
00:46:28,119 --> 00:46:30,705
I'm 99% sure I'll win.

946
00:46:31,539 --> 00:46:34,166
[Ddolddol] Of all people,
it was Jieun, who's a girl,

947
00:46:34,250 --> 00:46:36,585
and Joonsu, the youngest member,

948
00:46:37,169 --> 00:46:39,505
so I felt a little bad.

949
00:46:39,588 --> 00:46:41,590
Why? Because I know they're done for.

950
00:46:41,674 --> 00:46:42,675
[chuckles]

951
00:46:43,676 --> 00:46:45,219
[mic feedback]

952
00:46:45,303 --> 00:46:47,680
[host] The loser of this Death Match

953
00:46:49,932 --> 00:46:51,684
will become the first person eliminated,

954
00:46:52,601 --> 00:46:55,563
and they will leave Deadly Tag.

955
00:47:00,568 --> 00:47:02,778
[Joonsu] I'm going to return,
no matter what.

956
00:47:03,279 --> 00:47:04,989
I need to take everyone down now.

957
00:47:05,573 --> 00:47:07,116
[Jieun] I'll defeat everyone.

958
00:47:07,199 --> 00:47:09,618
[host] The first Death Match
of Deadly Tag is...

959
00:47:12,413 --> 00:47:13,789
"Time Case."

960
00:47:15,166 --> 00:47:16,417
-"Time Case"?
-"Time Case"?

961
00:47:16,500 --> 00:47:19,420
[host] "Time Case"
is a six-player survival game,

962
00:47:19,503 --> 00:47:22,214
in which time bombs
are hidden inside briefcases

963
00:47:22,298 --> 00:47:26,761
and players must avoid
the case that explodes first.

964
00:47:27,636 --> 00:47:30,222
The game will consist of two rounds.

965
00:47:31,098 --> 00:47:34,185
The game area consists of six zones.

966
00:47:34,727 --> 00:47:35,853
ZONE 1

967
00:47:35,936 --> 00:47:37,438
ZONE 2

968
00:47:37,521 --> 00:47:39,023
ZONE 3

969
00:47:39,106 --> 00:47:40,608
ZONE 4

970
00:47:40,691 --> 00:47:42,193
ZONE 5

971
00:47:42,818 --> 00:47:44,111
ZONE 6

972
00:47:44,195 --> 00:47:46,280
Once Round 1 begins,

973
00:47:46,364 --> 00:47:49,033
starting from the player
most recently eliminated,

974
00:47:49,116 --> 00:47:50,951
players will choose their cases.

975
00:47:51,035 --> 00:47:52,912
The number on the case they choose

976
00:47:52,995 --> 00:47:54,288
will become their zone.

977
00:47:54,997 --> 00:47:57,666
The time inside the cases
will not be revealed.

978
00:47:58,417 --> 00:48:00,127
But in Round 1,

979
00:48:00,211 --> 00:48:02,963
there are two cases
with the shortest times,

980
00:48:03,047 --> 00:48:05,424
and that time is 45 minutes.

981
00:48:06,717 --> 00:48:09,387
The moment a case hits zero
and explodes...

982
00:48:09,470 --> 00:48:11,889
-[explodes loudly]
-...the player holding that case

983
00:48:11,972 --> 00:48:15,351
or the player whose zone the case is in

984
00:48:15,434 --> 00:48:17,186
will be eliminated immediately.

985
00:48:17,269 --> 00:48:19,230
PASS THE CASE
TO SOMEONE ELSE TO SURVIVE

986
00:48:19,313 --> 00:48:23,234
Players can only move cases
that have entered their own zones.

987
00:48:23,317 --> 00:48:26,904
Once a case is moved
to another player's zone,

988
00:48:26,987 --> 00:48:31,158
the remaining time will be displayed
on the case for five seconds.

989
00:48:31,242 --> 00:48:35,413
Each zone can have up to two cases
moved into it.

990
00:48:36,580 --> 00:48:40,209
However, if a player holds two cases
for more than three minutes,

991
00:48:40,292 --> 00:48:42,753
their case-holding capacity
will increase by one slot,

992
00:48:42,837 --> 00:48:45,881
allowing them to hold up to three cases.

993
00:48:47,425 --> 00:48:48,843
In Round 2,

994
00:48:48,926 --> 00:48:51,846
all cases will be set to the same minute,

995
00:48:52,763 --> 00:48:55,182
but the seconds will be set differently.

996
00:48:56,142 --> 00:48:57,351
This is hard.

997
00:48:57,435 --> 00:48:59,520
[host] In Round 2,

998
00:48:59,603 --> 00:49:02,565
new cases will randomly appear
on the map during the game.

999
00:49:02,648 --> 00:49:07,027
These cases give players an advantage
when attacking other players.

1000
00:49:08,362 --> 00:49:10,698
One player will be eliminated in Round 1,

1001
00:49:10,781 --> 00:49:14,535
and another will be eliminated in Round 2.

1002
00:49:15,494 --> 00:49:18,497
[sighs] I want to pray,
but who am I supposed to pray to?

1003
00:49:18,581 --> 00:49:21,500
[Ddolddol] I think the most crucial thing
was zone selection.

1004
00:49:21,584 --> 00:49:25,379
If you're in a zone
with too many nearby zones,

1005
00:49:25,463 --> 00:49:27,381
they're likely to bring the cases to me.

1006
00:49:27,465 --> 00:49:29,216
They didn't know

1007
00:49:29,300 --> 00:49:32,511
we played the Dogs and Wolves game
in this area.

1008
00:49:32,595 --> 00:49:36,724
I could see the entire map
and all the timers in a single glance.

1009
00:49:36,807 --> 00:49:38,642
[Dail] Physical strength
isn't that crucial in this game.

1010
00:49:38,726 --> 00:49:40,060
Once you decide on your target,

1011
00:49:40,144 --> 00:49:41,896
knowing how long it takes to get to them,

1012
00:49:41,979 --> 00:49:45,691
knowing how much time they have before
they can move the case somewhere else,

1013
00:49:45,774 --> 00:49:48,319
and remembering that
are much more important.

1014
00:49:48,402 --> 00:49:50,779
After going through different scenarios
in my head,

1015
00:49:50,863 --> 00:49:53,032
it turned out to be pretty easy.

1016
00:49:53,115 --> 00:49:56,911
[host] We will now begin
with case selection.

1017
00:49:56,994 --> 00:49:59,079
Starting with Lee Joonsu,

1018
00:49:59,163 --> 00:50:00,831
please enter the room one by one.

1019
00:50:00,915 --> 00:50:02,750
JOONSU GOES FIRST
AS MOST RECENT ELIMINATION

1020
00:50:03,501 --> 00:50:05,252
DEALER ROOM

1021
00:50:05,878 --> 00:50:08,380
Mr. Lee Joonsu, please select a case.

1022
00:50:08,464 --> 00:50:09,924
Ah...

1023
00:50:10,007 --> 00:50:11,467
Let's see. No. 2, No. 1.

1024
00:50:12,092 --> 00:50:14,803
No. 1, No. 2, No. 1, No. 2, No. 4.

1025
00:50:16,805 --> 00:50:18,849
JOONSU'S CHOICE

1026
00:50:18,933 --> 00:50:21,393
[dealer] Please proceed to Zone 4.

1027
00:50:22,853 --> 00:50:24,605
-[Jieun] Which one did you pick? No. 4?
-No. 4.

1028
00:50:25,648 --> 00:50:27,566
Ms. Shin Jieun, please select a case.

1029
00:50:28,567 --> 00:50:29,568
No. 4?

1030
00:50:31,111 --> 00:50:32,613
[sighs] No. 1...

1031
00:50:32,696 --> 00:50:34,114
[inhales sharply]

1032
00:50:35,407 --> 00:50:38,369
[dealer] Ms. Shin Jieun
has selected Case No. 1.

1033
00:50:38,452 --> 00:50:42,915
[Jieun] I placed myself
somewhere close to Joonsu on purpose,

1034
00:50:42,998 --> 00:50:47,545
because we'd already agreed
that we'd work together.

1035
00:50:47,628 --> 00:50:51,048
If teamwork is going to matter
in this game,

1036
00:50:51,131 --> 00:50:54,260
I thought you would be the better choice.

1037
00:50:54,343 --> 00:50:55,886
That's partly why I chose you.

1038
00:50:55,970 --> 00:50:57,012
JIEUN PROPOSES AN ALLIANCE

1039
00:50:57,096 --> 00:50:58,764
-[Joonsu] I'll crush everyone.
-I won't be scared.

1040
00:50:58,847 --> 00:51:02,101
[Jieun] Don't make it obvious
we're allied.

1041
00:51:02,184 --> 00:51:04,103
We'll be outnumbered.

1042
00:51:04,186 --> 00:51:06,355
Let's pretend we're not on the same side.

1043
00:51:06,438 --> 00:51:08,065
Let's stab them in the back.

1044
00:51:08,148 --> 00:51:09,149
Okay.

1045
00:51:10,442 --> 00:51:11,443
[Jieun] Joonsu.

1046
00:51:11,527 --> 00:51:13,153
Meet me here when it starts.

1047
00:51:13,237 --> 00:51:14,321
Meet me here.

1048
00:51:17,533 --> 00:51:21,245
[Ddolddol] For Round 1,
I was going to head to a corner by myself.

1049
00:51:21,328 --> 00:51:25,040
Thankfully, they picked No. 1 and No. 4.

1050
00:51:25,124 --> 00:51:27,710
The most isolated one, Zone 6, was empty.

1051
00:51:27,793 --> 00:51:29,211
I immediately picked No. 6.

1052
00:51:29,295 --> 00:51:30,296
KIM DDOLDDOL, ZONE 6

1053
00:51:30,879 --> 00:51:33,757
[dealer] Mr. Yang Dail
has selected Case No. 5.

1054
00:51:33,841 --> 00:51:36,468
Mr. Pani Bottle, please proceed to Zone 3.

1055
00:51:37,136 --> 00:51:39,722
Ms. Gyeong Sujin,
please proceed to Zone 2.

1056
00:51:40,681 --> 00:51:43,392
CASES AND ZONES HAVE BEEN SELECTED

1057
00:51:43,475 --> 00:51:47,187
[host] We will now begin
Round 0 of "Time Case."

1058
00:51:47,271 --> 00:51:50,441
Round 0 is the item-collection round.

1059
00:51:51,191 --> 00:51:54,945
You'll have five minutes to pick up items.

1060
00:51:55,487 --> 00:51:57,615
The items are in the form of cards

1061
00:51:57,698 --> 00:51:58,991
labeled with numbers.

1062
00:52:00,034 --> 00:52:02,995
You can apply an item card
to a case with the same number

1063
00:52:04,121 --> 00:52:06,081
-to adjust its timer...
-[timer ticking]

1064
00:52:06,165 --> 00:52:07,583
...and decrease it up to three minutes

1065
00:52:07,666 --> 00:52:09,460
or add to it up to three minutes.

1066
00:52:10,628 --> 00:52:12,504
We will now begin

1067
00:52:12,588 --> 00:52:14,798
Round 0.

1068
00:52:14,882 --> 00:52:16,884
[♪ exciting music playing]

1069
00:52:27,978 --> 00:52:29,021
[Pani Bottle] Okay.

1070
00:52:30,314 --> 00:52:31,899
No. 6.

1071
00:52:31,982 --> 00:52:33,150
Items...

1072
00:52:33,233 --> 00:52:34,943
I thought it was important.

1073
00:52:35,027 --> 00:52:37,821
It's the only variable that allows us
to change the time

1074
00:52:37,905 --> 00:52:39,281
we were initially given.

1075
00:52:41,325 --> 00:52:42,451
[Sujin] Nothing.

1076
00:52:47,081 --> 00:52:49,416
I was able to collect two items.

1077
00:52:50,501 --> 00:52:53,796
MEANWHILE, DAIL IS FULL OF CONFIDENCE

1078
00:52:55,839 --> 00:52:58,133
-I got the path figured out.
-[Pani Bottle] How?

1079
00:52:58,217 --> 00:53:00,594
[Dail] Come straight out that steel door,
and I'm right there.

1080
00:53:00,678 --> 00:53:03,764
[Pani Bottle]
There are six cases at first.

1081
00:53:03,847 --> 00:53:05,683
If there are two cases with longer times,

1082
00:53:05,766 --> 00:53:07,518
-we could pass them among us.
-[Dail] Right.

1083
00:53:07,601 --> 00:53:08,852
[Pani Bottle] Let's trade.

1084
00:53:08,936 --> 00:53:10,646
Let's share the times first. Okay.

1085
00:53:10,729 --> 00:53:13,899
[Dail] Someone's going to share with me
how much time is left

1086
00:53:13,982 --> 00:53:15,776
on a certain case?

1087
00:53:15,859 --> 00:53:17,069
I felt so reassured.

1088
00:53:17,152 --> 00:53:18,278
PANI BOTTLE AND DAIL TEAM UP

1089
00:53:18,362 --> 00:53:22,366
We don't have any sharp advantages,
but together we make a really good team.

1090
00:53:22,449 --> 00:53:23,617
Like puzzle pieces.

1091
00:53:24,201 --> 00:53:26,537
[Dail] The important part for me
was analyzing the routes.

1092
00:53:26,620 --> 00:53:29,415
Like, figuring out which paths
between zones were faster.

1093
00:53:29,498 --> 00:53:33,335
Managing just three nearby zones

1094
00:53:33,419 --> 00:53:36,714
was already overwhelming
and stressful in the game.

1095
00:53:36,797 --> 00:53:37,923
No. 5.

1096
00:53:38,006 --> 00:53:39,383
DAIL CAREFULLY STUDIES THE MAP LAYOUT

1097
00:53:39,466 --> 00:53:40,759
Go straight, and it's Zone 2.

1098
00:53:42,010 --> 00:53:43,095
It's so damn far.

1099
00:53:45,180 --> 00:53:47,057
[alarm blaring]

1100
00:53:47,141 --> 00:53:50,519
[host] We will now start Round 1
of "Time Case."

1101
00:53:51,186 --> 00:53:54,440
You may now move the Time Cases.

1102
00:53:54,523 --> 00:53:55,524
CASE TIMERS ON

1103
00:53:56,608 --> 00:53:57,693
[Joonsu] Hold on.

1104
00:53:57,776 --> 00:53:59,737
-Let's trade cases.
-[Jieun] Okay.

1105
00:53:59,820 --> 00:54:01,780
TIMER SHOWS FOR 5 SECONDS
IN ANOTHER PLAYER'S ZONE

1106
00:54:02,990 --> 00:54:03,991
ZONE 4
JOONSU'S ZONE

1107
00:54:04,074 --> 00:54:05,159
[Joonsu] How many minutes?

1108
00:54:06,326 --> 00:54:07,453
-Okay.
-[Jieun] It's 43 minutes.

1109
00:54:07,536 --> 00:54:08,537
[sighs]

1110
00:54:09,413 --> 00:54:10,748
Okay.

1111
00:54:10,831 --> 00:54:12,666
ZONE 3
PANI BOTTLE'S ZONE

1112
00:54:14,168 --> 00:54:15,169
Good.

1113
00:54:15,252 --> 00:54:16,920
ZONE 5
DAIL'S ZONE

1114
00:54:17,504 --> 00:54:18,714
It's 50 minutes. What's mine?

1115
00:54:18,797 --> 00:54:20,466
-It's 44 minutes.
-44 minutes?

1116
00:54:20,549 --> 00:54:21,717
ZONE 2
SUJIN'S ZONE

1117
00:54:23,552 --> 00:54:24,845
[Pani Bottle] Ddolddol!

1118
00:54:26,180 --> 00:54:28,015
Kim Ddolddol!

1119
00:54:28,098 --> 00:54:30,100
Yes, I'm right here.

1120
00:54:30,184 --> 00:54:31,310
-[Pani Bottle] Hold on.
-What?

1121
00:54:31,393 --> 00:54:33,687
[Pani Bottle] The best way
is to check the time and share it.

1122
00:54:33,771 --> 00:54:35,147
[Ddolddol] Right.

1123
00:54:35,230 --> 00:54:37,357
-[Pani Bottle] Tell me the time.
-What's the time now?

1124
00:54:37,441 --> 00:54:38,525
THE TWO SHARE TIMER INFORMATION

1125
00:54:38,609 --> 00:54:42,154
I believed Ddolddol would be
a reliable teammate I could count on.

1126
00:54:42,237 --> 00:54:43,572
So I asked him for help.

1127
00:54:43,655 --> 00:54:44,990
No. 4 has a lot of time left.

1128
00:54:45,073 --> 00:54:46,575
-There's 47 minutes.
-[Pani Bottle] Okay.

1129
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:49,703
-[Ddolddol] This is 50 minutes.
-[Pani Bottle] No. 6? That's long. What?

1130
00:54:49,786 --> 00:54:51,872
Is it No. 5? No. 5 is the shortest.

1131
00:54:51,955 --> 00:54:53,415
No. 5 is the shortest? Okay.

1132
00:54:56,251 --> 00:54:58,128
THE CASES WITH THE SHORTEST TIMES

1133
00:54:59,338 --> 00:55:01,632
CASE 1
45 MINUTES

1134
00:55:01,715 --> 00:55:03,884
CASE 5
45 MINUTES

1135
00:55:03,967 --> 00:55:08,222
The first priority was figuring out
which cases had the shortest times left.

1136
00:55:08,305 --> 00:55:12,309
If I got the time bomb case
in either No. 1 or No. 5,

1137
00:55:12,392 --> 00:55:15,938
the key is where I place it
when it has only one minute left.

1138
00:55:16,021 --> 00:55:18,774
That's how I could eliminate someone.

1139
00:55:19,691 --> 00:55:21,443
I had a rough idea of the timers.

1140
00:55:21,527 --> 00:55:23,362
I walked around the game area.

1141
00:55:25,113 --> 00:55:26,240
Look.

1142
00:55:27,950 --> 00:55:30,577
Look at the map.
These areas are at a disadvantage.

1143
00:55:30,661 --> 00:55:32,829
Areas right in the middle,
like Zones 2 and 3.

1144
00:55:33,413 --> 00:55:36,583
ZONES 2 AND 3 ARE EASY TARGETS

1145
00:55:37,417 --> 00:55:38,418
ZONE 2, ZONE 3

1146
00:55:38,502 --> 00:55:40,754
THE MIDDLE ZONES ARE NEXT TO EACH OTHER

1147
00:55:41,505 --> 00:55:43,590
I thought, "This is not good."

1148
00:55:43,674 --> 00:55:46,218
ANXIOUS

1149
00:55:46,301 --> 00:55:48,095
I didn't want to be eliminated.

1150
00:55:48,178 --> 00:55:51,098
I was so desperate to stay in the game.

1151
00:55:52,307 --> 00:55:54,434
What we picked put us at a disadvantage.

1152
00:55:54,518 --> 00:55:56,311
We need to get rid of Gyeong Sujin.

1153
00:55:57,104 --> 00:55:59,189
GYEONG SUJIN APPEARS

1154
00:56:02,234 --> 00:56:05,195
In fact, while Sujin was in jail,

1155
00:56:05,279 --> 00:56:06,780
she suspected we might be the Seeker.

1156
00:56:08,073 --> 00:56:11,285
PANI BOTTLE WAS WORRIED
ABOUT SUJIN'S SUSPICIONS

1157
00:56:11,368 --> 00:56:13,662
We figured it wouldn't do any good
to keep her around.

1158
00:56:14,580 --> 00:56:16,415
[Dail] I agree with that too.

1159
00:56:17,374 --> 00:56:20,419
We'll have no choice
but to have her eliminated.

1160
00:56:20,502 --> 00:56:21,503
I realized that.

1161
00:56:21,587 --> 00:56:25,090
SUJIN SUDDENLY BECOMES A TARGET

1162
00:56:32,723 --> 00:56:33,724
Ddolddol!

1163
00:56:35,684 --> 00:56:36,810
[whispers] Come over here.

1164
00:56:39,521 --> 00:56:41,690
The Seeker is a player from prison.

1165
00:56:41,773 --> 00:56:43,525
-Really?
-Yes.

1166
00:56:44,818 --> 00:56:45,819
The reason why

1167
00:56:46,737 --> 00:56:50,073
I'm only telling you this
is because you're not a Seeker.

1168
00:56:50,157 --> 00:56:51,158
Just so you know.

1169
00:56:53,243 --> 00:56:54,369
[Ddolddol breathes deeply]

1170
00:56:54,453 --> 00:56:58,165
[Sujin] I thought I needed
to get inside people's heads.

1171
00:57:01,293 --> 00:57:02,628
APPROACHING JIEUN THIS TIME

1172
00:57:02,711 --> 00:57:03,837
Excuse me.

1173
00:57:03,920 --> 00:57:06,089
You know I'm not a Seeker, right?

1174
00:57:06,173 --> 00:57:07,674
-[Jieun] Yes.
-I really am not.

1175
00:57:09,259 --> 00:57:11,094
We have to catch the Seeker.

1176
00:57:11,178 --> 00:57:14,473
The ultimate goal of this game
is to catch the Seeker.

1177
00:57:15,057 --> 00:57:18,185
I was taken off
the list of possible Seekers

1178
00:57:18,268 --> 00:57:19,478
from the very beginning.

1179
00:57:19,561 --> 00:57:22,230
That's why they shouldn't eliminate me.

1180
00:57:22,981 --> 00:57:24,191
No one would doubt that.

1181
00:57:24,274 --> 00:57:25,359
IS IT A BLUFF OR THE TRUTH?

1182
00:57:25,442 --> 00:57:28,445
No one would suspect
that the person in prison was the Seeker.

1183
00:57:31,740 --> 00:57:34,618
[host] There are two Time Cases in Zone 2.

1184
00:57:35,786 --> 00:57:37,871
[Sujin] Here we go. This is serious.

1185
00:57:39,748 --> 00:57:44,252
THE ATTACKS BEGIN

1186
00:57:45,212 --> 00:57:48,006
If you leave two cases
for more than three minutes,

1187
00:57:48,090 --> 00:57:51,093
the number of slots goes up by one,
which makes things worse.

1188
00:57:51,176 --> 00:57:53,261
For that, I kept dropping cases
into her zone.

1189
00:57:53,345 --> 00:57:57,140
It was to check things out, to attack,
and to increase Sujin's slots.

1190
00:57:57,224 --> 00:57:59,226
It is what it is. This is about survival.

1191
00:58:01,019 --> 00:58:03,313
ONCE A CASE IS PLACED,
ONLY THE ZONE'S OWNER CAN MOVE IT

1192
00:58:03,397 --> 00:58:04,564
Trade, trade.

1193
00:58:06,441 --> 00:58:07,609
We'll exchange anyway.

1194
00:58:07,693 --> 00:58:09,027
First off, just attack.

1195
00:58:12,239 --> 00:58:14,116
[Sujin] This is exhausting. [pants]

1196
00:58:14,908 --> 00:58:18,078
TO SURVIVE, PASS THE CASE ON

1197
00:58:20,372 --> 00:58:23,500
[host] There are two Time Cases in Zone 2.

1198
00:58:26,420 --> 00:58:27,421
[exhales]

1199
00:58:27,504 --> 00:58:28,797
[Sujin sighs]

1200
00:58:29,715 --> 00:58:32,843
There are two Time Cases in Zone 2.

1201
00:58:32,926 --> 00:58:36,263
I heard "Zone 2" so many times
that it got stuck in my head.

1202
00:58:41,017 --> 00:58:45,522
JOONSU WATCHES IT ALL UNFOLD

1203
00:58:48,275 --> 00:58:50,610
[Joonsu] There were barrels
in front of her zone,

1204
00:58:50,694 --> 00:58:54,030
so I set them down
to make it harder for them to move around.

1205
00:58:56,867 --> 00:59:00,328
[host] There are two Time Cases in Zone 2.

1206
00:59:00,412 --> 00:59:02,831
Come on, don't do this. What's with them?

1207
00:59:04,374 --> 00:59:05,500
[exhales frustratedly]

1208
00:59:05,584 --> 00:59:07,002
I got really mad.

1209
00:59:12,632 --> 00:59:15,218
JOONSU BLOCKS THE PATH WITH THE BARREL

1210
00:59:15,302 --> 00:59:16,887
[Joonsu] I had to do
what needed to be done.

1211
00:59:16,970 --> 00:59:18,096
I have to survive.

1212
00:59:25,645 --> 00:59:26,646
[thuds]

1213
00:59:27,147 --> 00:59:28,440
[Sujin] Excuse me.

1214
00:59:28,523 --> 00:59:30,358
What do you think you're doing?

1215
00:59:34,279 --> 00:59:36,031
[Dail] I didn't do that.

1216
00:59:37,115 --> 00:59:39,493
[Sujin] Is this how they're trying to win?

1217
00:59:39,576 --> 00:59:41,161
I understand. It's a game, after all.

1218
00:59:41,244 --> 00:59:42,412
Fine, let's see

1219
00:59:43,079 --> 00:59:44,080
who wins in the end.

1220
00:59:44,164 --> 00:59:46,583
SUJIN APPROACHES JIEUN

1221
00:59:47,000 --> 00:59:48,460
-We need to put...
-[Jieun] Yes?

1222
00:59:48,543 --> 00:59:49,961
[Sujin] ...two cases in Dail's zone.

1223
00:59:50,045 --> 00:59:51,421
I've got a plan.

1224
00:59:51,505 --> 00:59:52,631
SUJIN'S TARGET IS DAIL

1225
00:59:52,714 --> 00:59:55,550
[Jieun] Keep putting them there?
Got it. I'll place it there.

1226
01:00:00,555 --> 01:00:01,681
SUJIN WALKS PAST DAIL

1227
01:00:01,765 --> 01:00:03,683
[Dail] Every time we crossed paths,

1228
01:00:05,352 --> 01:00:08,522
I worried, "What if she puts the bomb
on me at the end?"

1229
01:00:09,105 --> 01:00:10,982
It felt so unfair.

1230
01:00:11,066 --> 01:00:12,484
The more time passed,

1231
01:00:12,567 --> 01:00:14,986
the more it felt like it'd come down
to a last-second battle.

1232
01:00:15,070 --> 01:00:18,240
NO. 1 AND NO. 5 WILL EXPLODE IN 12 MINUTES

1233
01:00:18,323 --> 01:00:19,407
Do you know where No. 1 and 5 are?

1234
01:00:19,491 --> 01:00:22,160
-No. 1 and 5 have the shortest time left.
-[Dail] No. 1, 5?

1235
01:00:22,244 --> 01:00:23,453
We need to know where they are.

1236
01:00:24,204 --> 01:00:25,288
No. 1, No. 5. No. 1, No. 5.

1237
01:00:25,372 --> 01:00:27,123
CASE NO. 1 AND NO. 5 GO MISSING

1238
01:00:27,874 --> 01:00:31,628
[host] There are two Time Cases in Zone 6.

1239
01:00:31,711 --> 01:00:33,922
[Pani Bottle] I think
they're at Zone 6. Hold on.

1240
01:00:34,005 --> 01:00:35,298
[groans] Fuck!

1241
01:00:38,093 --> 01:00:39,594
Ddolddol!

1242
01:00:40,887 --> 01:00:42,013
Ddolddol.

1243
01:00:42,806 --> 01:00:43,849
Ddolddol!

1244
01:00:48,854 --> 01:00:49,855
Where did he go?

1245
01:00:51,857 --> 01:00:52,899
Ddolddol!

1246
01:00:54,150 --> 01:00:55,944
Hang on, what's going on? Something's off.

1247
01:00:56,027 --> 01:00:57,362
Where is he?

1248
01:00:59,698 --> 01:01:00,699
[Dail] Pani Bottle.

1249
01:01:01,241 --> 01:01:02,242
[Pani Bottle] Dail.

1250
01:01:03,034 --> 01:01:04,744
Have you seen Ddolddol?

1251
01:01:04,828 --> 01:01:06,329
-[Dail] I haven't.
-Where is he?

1252
01:01:06,413 --> 01:01:07,414
PANI BOTTLE AND DAIL ARE CONFUSED

1253
01:01:07,497 --> 01:01:09,583
Do you know where No. 1 and No. 5 are?

1254
01:01:09,666 --> 01:01:11,001
[Pani Bottle] I think they're at Zone 6.

1255
01:01:13,336 --> 01:01:16,798
We need to find out
who's holding No. 1 and 5.

1256
01:01:16,882 --> 01:01:18,008
[Pani Bottle sighs frustratedly]

1257
01:01:18,091 --> 01:01:20,093
[♪ mysterious music playing]

1258
01:01:23,305 --> 01:01:30,312
SOMEONE'S HIDING THE CASES ON PURPOSE?

1259
01:01:32,564 --> 01:01:35,025
[panting]

1260
01:01:40,196 --> 01:01:41,823
[Sujin] They were all in my zone.

1261
01:01:50,999 --> 01:01:54,544
JOONSU WAS PASSING BY SUJIN'S ZONE

1262
01:01:55,003 --> 01:01:56,379
[Pani Bottle] Joonsu.

1263
01:01:57,255 --> 01:01:59,341
Both No. 1 and No. 5
are in Zone 2 right now.

1264
01:01:59,424 --> 01:02:00,425
-In Sujin's zone.
-[Pani Bottle] No.

1265
01:02:00,508 --> 01:02:03,637
[breathing heavily]

1266
01:02:10,393 --> 01:02:12,228
They can't come to me at the end.

1267
01:02:12,312 --> 01:02:15,315
[Dail] I realized
I really needed to stay alert.

1268
01:02:16,608 --> 01:02:20,028
IT'S FINALLY TIME TO MAKE A MOVE

1269
01:02:27,911 --> 01:02:28,912
PANI BOTTLE VISITS DAIL

1270
01:02:28,995 --> 01:02:32,082
-Are you sure? That this...
-No. 5 has 20 minutes on it.

1271
01:02:32,165 --> 01:02:34,042
-If it's shorter...
-Then leave No. 4 to me.

1272
01:02:34,125 --> 01:02:35,919
-Leave it to me now.
-Right now?

1273
01:02:36,002 --> 01:02:39,214
DAIL TAKES OFF AT PANI BOTTLE'S REQUEST

1274
01:02:46,388 --> 01:02:48,765
SUJIN'S TARGET IS DAIL

1275
01:02:48,848 --> 01:02:52,227
[host] There are two Time Cases in Zone 5.

1276
01:02:54,521 --> 01:02:55,522
[Ddolddol] Be careful.

1277
01:02:55,605 --> 01:02:57,607
RUNNING IN PANIC

1278
01:03:21,172 --> 01:03:23,174
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1279
01:03:28,388 --> 01:03:30,724
[timer ticking]

1280
01:03:35,353 --> 01:03:36,354
[exhales]

1281
01:03:36,438 --> 01:03:38,440
[panting]

1282
01:03:42,068 --> 01:03:44,070
[timer ticking]

1283
01:03:44,154 --> 01:03:47,449
THE TIME ON CASE NO. 1 SUDDENLY DROPS

1284
01:03:47,532 --> 01:03:49,826
[Dail] What the heck? I'm fucked.

1285
01:03:49,909 --> 01:03:51,953
ONLY TWO MINUTES UNTIL EXPLOSION

1286
01:03:52,537 --> 01:03:53,705
What kind of bastard...

1287
01:03:54,622 --> 01:03:56,708
I'm so fucked.

1288
01:03:57,584 --> 01:04:00,295
EARLIER

1289
01:04:01,921 --> 01:04:03,381
DEALER ROOM

1290
01:04:03,465 --> 01:04:05,425
[Sujin] I went to the Dealer Room

1291
01:04:06,676 --> 01:04:07,886
and shortened the time.

1292
01:04:09,179 --> 01:04:10,847
Minus three minutes on Case No. 1.

1293
01:04:12,515 --> 01:04:14,392
[panting]

1294
01:04:15,268 --> 01:04:18,188
Geez, all the cases
with the shortest times are coming to me.

1295
01:04:19,189 --> 01:04:20,982
I thought I might actually lose.

1296
01:04:21,066 --> 01:04:23,068
[breathing heavily]

1297
01:04:30,533 --> 01:04:33,244
Sujin kept leaving the cases in my zone.

1298
01:04:33,870 --> 01:04:37,415
If I played smart, I still had a chance
to turn things around.

1299
01:04:45,381 --> 01:04:47,926
To buy as much time as possible
before she could reach me,

1300
01:04:48,009 --> 01:04:49,052
I had to go a little far.

1301
01:04:49,135 --> 01:04:51,012
So I dragged things out with Case No. 1.

1302
01:04:51,096 --> 01:04:52,972
I stalled with Case No. 1.

1303
01:04:53,723 --> 01:04:58,436
-[panting]
-[timer ticking]

1304
01:04:58,520 --> 01:05:01,106
[timer beeping]

1305
01:05:01,189 --> 01:05:03,233
ONE MINUTE BEFORE EXPLOSION

1306
01:05:05,819 --> 01:05:08,196
[breathes heavily]

1307
01:05:08,279 --> 01:05:09,489
They should come this way.

1308
01:05:09,572 --> 01:05:11,074
[footsteps]

1309
01:05:18,039 --> 01:05:19,374
JIEUN'S ZONE AND NOT SUJIN'S

1310
01:05:19,457 --> 01:05:22,210
For me, the farthest place
was Jieun's zone,

1311
01:05:22,293 --> 01:05:23,461
so I passed through Joonsu

1312
01:05:23,545 --> 01:05:24,879
and dropped it over at Jieun's.

1313
01:05:27,632 --> 01:05:29,634
[timer beeping rapidly]

1314
01:05:33,429 --> 01:05:34,973
[case explodes]

1315
01:05:37,392 --> 01:05:39,144
[Sujin panting]

1316
01:05:40,395 --> 01:05:41,521
[sighs]

1317
01:05:41,604 --> 01:05:44,858
[host] Gyeong Sujin's Time Case
has exploded.

1318
01:05:45,817 --> 01:05:48,528
1 MINUTE AGO

1319
01:05:50,446 --> 01:05:54,159
[Jieun] I could actually see Dail hiding.

1320
01:05:54,242 --> 01:05:57,537
But it felt like
he was trying to stall for time.

1321
01:05:57,620 --> 01:05:59,831
So I pretended to leave the area.

1322
01:06:08,548 --> 01:06:10,758
The case had 44 seconds left.

1323
01:06:12,760 --> 01:06:15,597
I didn't have time to think.

1324
01:06:17,307 --> 01:06:20,393
I thought I had to take out
whoever was closest to me.

1325
01:06:20,476 --> 01:06:22,687
That happened to be Sujin.

1326
01:06:22,770 --> 01:06:25,231
NOT ENOUGH TIME TO GET BACK AT DAIL

1327
01:06:25,315 --> 01:06:26,482
[panting]

1328
01:06:26,566 --> 01:06:28,443
Where's the case? Case No. 1.

1329
01:06:31,196 --> 01:06:32,322
No way.

1330
01:06:32,405 --> 01:06:35,200
I went back thinking, "No way."

1331
01:06:38,036 --> 01:06:39,245
Which case is it?

1332
01:06:39,329 --> 01:06:40,371
No. 1.

1333
01:06:40,455 --> 01:06:41,706
[Sujin] Not No. 1.

1334
01:06:42,332 --> 01:06:43,333
I'm screwed.

1335
01:06:44,918 --> 01:06:47,712
I was taken out by the card I used.

1336
01:06:50,131 --> 01:06:51,132
[clicks tongue]

1337
01:06:51,716 --> 01:06:53,635
[sighs] This is where it ends for me.

1338
01:06:53,718 --> 01:06:55,053
[mic feedback]

1339
01:06:55,136 --> 01:06:56,804
[host] Round 1 is over.

1340
01:06:57,305 --> 01:06:59,557
[Dail groans]
that was brutal as hell. [sighs]

1341
01:07:00,892 --> 01:07:02,810
[sighs, groans]

1342
01:07:03,728 --> 01:07:04,729
[sighs]

1343
01:07:08,942 --> 01:07:09,943
[gasps]

1344
01:07:10,735 --> 01:07:13,738
[host] Before we begin Round 2
of "Time Case,"

1345
01:07:14,656 --> 01:07:17,742
due to her Time Case exploding,
Gyeong Sujin

1346
01:07:17,825 --> 01:07:21,079
-has been eliminated.
-[exclaims]

1347
01:07:21,996 --> 01:07:23,998
[♪ somber music playing]

1348
01:07:29,087 --> 01:07:31,256
Good work, everyone.

1349
01:07:31,965 --> 01:07:34,550
-Good job, everyone.
-[Sujin] That was a great game.

1350
01:07:35,635 --> 01:07:36,761
[sighs]

1351
01:07:38,012 --> 01:07:40,265
Hope you make it to the end.

1352
01:07:40,348 --> 01:07:43,309
Sujin, it's really a misunderstanding.
I swear, I didn't block it.

1353
01:07:43,393 --> 01:07:44,644
It really wasn't me. Trust me.

1354
01:07:44,727 --> 01:07:46,104
FIRST ELIMINATION IS GYEONG SUJIN

1355
01:07:46,187 --> 01:07:47,855
-[Joonsu] Good work.
-Let's have a drink later.

1356
01:07:48,356 --> 01:07:49,357
[Sujin chuckles]

1357
01:07:52,652 --> 01:07:54,320
[Jieun] I felt so bad for her.

1358
01:07:57,407 --> 01:08:00,243
[Ddolddol] I was really sad
when I heard Sujin was out.

1359
01:08:01,411 --> 01:08:03,204
[Dail] Thank you, and sorry, Sujin.

1360
01:08:03,913 --> 01:08:05,498
But I had no choice.

1361
01:08:05,581 --> 01:08:07,500
I came here to survive,

1362
01:08:08,126 --> 01:08:09,836
so I had to put my survival first.

1363
01:08:10,962 --> 01:08:14,007
[host] We will now begin
with case selection for Round 2.

1364
01:08:14,090 --> 01:08:15,091
TIME CASE ROUND 2

1365
01:08:15,174 --> 01:08:18,303
In Round 2, the seconds for every case

1366
01:08:18,386 --> 01:08:20,263
will be set at different times.

1367
01:08:20,763 --> 01:08:24,726
We will now start
Time Case selection to change zones.

1368
01:08:25,935 --> 01:08:27,562
Excluding Gyeong Sujin,

1369
01:08:27,645 --> 01:08:31,983
we will start with the player holding
the case with the shortest remaining time.

1370
01:08:33,443 --> 01:08:35,862
Shin Jieun, please enter first.

1371
01:08:35,945 --> 01:08:37,530
[Jieun] This works in my favor.

1372
01:08:37,613 --> 01:08:40,241
I thought I had to make the most
of this opportunity.

1373
01:08:40,325 --> 01:08:41,451
[clears throat, sniffles]

1374
01:08:41,534 --> 01:08:42,702
How many cards do you have?

1375
01:08:42,785 --> 01:08:44,287
Do we have two cases coming in?

1376
01:08:44,370 --> 01:08:45,413
RIGHT AFTER JIEUN LEAVES

1377
01:08:45,496 --> 01:08:46,789
-One, right?
-Two will spawn.

1378
01:08:46,873 --> 01:08:49,459
Listen. Just keep your own case
and stay where you are.

1379
01:08:49,542 --> 01:08:51,210
-I know.
-[Ddolddol] When someone comes over,

1380
01:08:51,294 --> 01:08:52,587
we rotate it and check the time.

1381
01:08:52,670 --> 01:08:55,548
We need to keep sharing the timer
on the two cases that respawn.

1382
01:08:55,631 --> 01:08:57,884
-Then repeat.
-Let's pass the cases around among us.

1383
01:08:58,760 --> 01:09:00,762
[♪ tense music playing]

1384
01:09:03,681 --> 01:09:04,682
[sniffles]

1385
01:09:06,809 --> 01:09:09,937
[Joonsu] I really just stayed still
because I was scared.

1386
01:09:14,567 --> 01:09:17,195
If you were in my position,
you'd understand.

1387
01:09:18,780 --> 01:09:21,115
I had only one thought in my head.

1388
01:09:21,199 --> 01:09:22,617
Win, no matter what.

1389
01:09:22,700 --> 01:09:24,160
That's all I could think of.

1390
01:09:24,744 --> 01:09:27,246
Ms. Shin Jieun, please select a Time Case.

1391
01:09:27,830 --> 01:09:29,207
This one.

1392
01:09:31,459 --> 01:09:33,669
-Put anything that spawns there.
-Exactly.

1393
01:09:33,753 --> 01:09:35,254
TALKS QUICKLY END WHEN JIEUN RETURNS

1394
01:09:35,338 --> 01:09:36,422
That should be safer.

1395
01:09:36,506 --> 01:09:37,757
-I'm always worried.
-[Jieun] I'm cold.

1396
01:09:37,840 --> 01:09:39,008
[hisses]

1397
01:09:39,092 --> 01:09:40,093
[clears throat]

1398
01:09:40,676 --> 01:09:45,223
[Jieun] Zone 6 was more isolated
than the other areas.

1399
01:09:45,306 --> 01:09:47,892
I didn't want to rule out the possibility

1400
01:09:47,975 --> 01:09:52,021
that they could attack whoever was closest

1401
01:09:52,105 --> 01:09:54,982
if they fell into an emergency situation.

1402
01:09:55,066 --> 01:09:57,443
I thought it was absolutely worth a shot.

1403
01:09:58,569 --> 01:10:01,280
[host] Kim Ddolddol, please enter.

1404
01:10:01,364 --> 01:10:04,867
[dealer] Mr. Kim Ddolddol
has selected Case No. 4.

1405
01:10:04,951 --> 01:10:06,119
[Pani Bottle] I'll go with No. 5.

1406
01:10:06,202 --> 01:10:09,247
[dealer] Okay,
you have selected Case No. 5.

1407
01:10:09,330 --> 01:10:11,916
[host] Lee Joonsu, please enter.

1408
01:10:11,999 --> 01:10:13,710
I'm the last one. [sighs frustratedly]

1409
01:10:15,878 --> 01:10:18,131
What did Jieun choose? She chose...

1410
01:10:18,214 --> 01:10:19,590
Pani Bottle got No. 4.

1411
01:10:19,674 --> 01:10:20,925
Then...

1412
01:10:21,008 --> 01:10:24,178
I tried to choose a zone
that was as close as possible to Jieun.

1413
01:10:24,804 --> 01:10:26,264
I'll go with No. 3.

1414
01:10:27,181 --> 01:10:29,726
[dealer] Mr. Lee Joonsu,
you have selected Case No. 3.

1415
01:10:29,809 --> 01:10:30,810
Thank you.

1416
01:10:30,893 --> 01:10:32,895
Mr. Yang Dail, there's only one case left.

1417
01:10:32,979 --> 01:10:33,980
Okay.

1418
01:10:34,480 --> 01:10:35,481
Case No. 2.

1419
01:10:35,565 --> 01:10:38,818
DAIL TAKES CASE NO. 2

1420
01:10:39,569 --> 01:10:42,613
ROUND 2 CASES AND ZONES HAVE BEEN SELECTED

1421
01:10:42,697 --> 01:10:44,615
[alarm blaring]

1422
01:10:45,950 --> 01:10:50,163
[host] Round 2 of "Time Case"
will begin now.

1423
01:10:53,875 --> 01:10:55,501
[Pani Bottle]
Leave it here. Don't kill it.

1424
01:10:55,585 --> 01:10:56,669
ZONE 5
PANI BOTTLE'S ZONE

1425
01:10:56,753 --> 01:10:57,754
Don't kill it.

1426
01:10:57,837 --> 01:11:01,048
[host] There are two Time Cases in Zone 5.

1427
01:11:01,632 --> 01:11:02,759
ZONE 2
DAIL'S ZONE

1428
01:11:04,302 --> 01:11:07,597
In Round 2, the seconds for every case
will be set at different times.

1429
01:11:07,680 --> 01:11:09,140
SHORTEST TIMES

1430
01:11:09,223 --> 01:11:11,225
[♪ tense music playing]

1431
01:11:15,438 --> 01:11:17,732
[Jieun] I looked around for a moment.

1432
01:11:19,233 --> 01:11:21,110
Judging by the atmosphere,

1433
01:11:21,778 --> 01:11:23,321
something felt a little off.

1434
01:11:27,158 --> 01:11:29,368
[coughs] Why is nothing here?

1435
01:11:30,620 --> 01:11:32,663
No one left cases in my area,

1436
01:11:32,747 --> 01:11:34,916
and it was unexpected.

1437
01:11:34,999 --> 01:11:38,294
DDOLDDOL IS STANDING IN PLACE

1438
01:11:44,008 --> 01:11:45,051
[Dail] Thirty minutes.

1439
01:11:45,134 --> 01:11:47,678
[Pani Bottle] We can't put it yet.
Three minutes have to pass.

1440
01:11:47,762 --> 01:11:48,971
Once three minutes pass,

1441
01:11:49,055 --> 01:11:50,056
-a notice pops up.
-Right.

1442
01:11:50,139 --> 01:11:52,475
[Pani Bottle] When it does,
just place it and we're done.

1443
01:11:52,558 --> 01:11:54,811
I went into Round 2 thinking,

1444
01:11:54,894 --> 01:11:56,437
"Even if I wanted to lose, I couldn't."

1445
01:11:56,521 --> 01:11:58,689
It was basically in the bag.
How could I possibly lose?

1446
01:11:58,773 --> 01:12:00,066
I can't possibly lose.

1447
01:12:00,149 --> 01:12:02,318
[Pani Bottle] As for the penalty,
there are two cases.

1448
01:12:02,401 --> 01:12:05,696
Once it passes three minutes,
you can place up to three cases.

1449
01:12:05,780 --> 01:12:07,031
It might seem like a bad thing,

1450
01:12:07,114 --> 01:12:10,034
but if three cases with long timers
come in, you can't put any more.

1451
01:12:10,117 --> 01:12:14,747
I'm not really the type
who understands game rules instantly.

1452
01:12:14,831 --> 01:12:19,585
[host] Each zone can have
up to two cases moved into it.

1453
01:12:19,669 --> 01:12:22,505
However, if a player holds two cases
for more than three minutes,

1454
01:12:22,588 --> 01:12:23,840
"WHAT EVERYONE THOUGHT WAS A PENALTY"

1455
01:12:23,923 --> 01:12:26,300
their case-holding capacity
will increase by one slot,

1456
01:12:26,384 --> 01:12:28,135
allowing them to hold up to three cases.

1457
01:12:28,219 --> 01:12:29,262
CAN'T PLACE ANY MORE CASES

1458
01:12:30,346 --> 01:12:33,975
[Pani Bottle] That's when I realized
I should take advantage of this

1459
01:12:34,058 --> 01:12:36,769
and block out cases.

1460
01:12:36,853 --> 01:12:39,564
I tested it out in Round 1.

1461
01:12:40,147 --> 01:12:41,816
When Sujin saw the cases in my area,

1462
01:12:41,899 --> 01:12:43,067
"HIS ZONE WAS FULL WITH THREE"

1463
01:12:43,943 --> 01:12:45,570
I saw her go, "Geez" and walk away.

1464
01:12:45,653 --> 01:12:47,738
I thought, "Okay, we got it."

1465
01:12:48,322 --> 01:12:50,908
Whether it was Yuk Junseo

1466
01:12:50,992 --> 01:12:52,118
or Horseking who came,

1467
01:12:52,201 --> 01:12:53,619
I could eliminate anyone.

1468
01:12:53,703 --> 01:12:54,787
It's a sure-win strategy.

1469
01:12:55,329 --> 01:12:58,165
It doesn't matter who goes first.
Just go and join Sujin.

1470
01:12:58,875 --> 01:13:01,836
ZONE 2
DAIL'S ZONE

1471
01:13:06,090 --> 01:13:07,466
[Ddolddol] Which number is it?

1472
01:13:07,550 --> 01:13:08,634
No. 6.

1473
01:13:08,718 --> 01:13:10,261
Jieun left it at my zone.

1474
01:13:10,344 --> 01:13:11,637
[Ddolddol] Is it hers?

1475
01:13:11,721 --> 01:13:13,681
[Dail] It's quite far from here.

1476
01:13:13,764 --> 01:13:16,684
We can't put two in your zone.
We should put them somewhere closer.

1477
01:13:16,767 --> 01:13:18,269
Then, they'll get fucked on the way.

1478
01:13:18,352 --> 01:13:20,771
[Ddolddol] What's the number of mine?
What's your number?

1479
01:13:20,855 --> 01:13:22,523
-No. 2?
-Yes, No. 2.

1480
01:13:23,024 --> 01:13:24,358
BLOCKING ZONE CHANGES BASED ON DAIL'S IDEA

1481
01:13:24,442 --> 01:13:26,402
-[Ddolddol] Is yours empty?
-It's empty.

1482
01:13:26,485 --> 01:13:29,530
ZONE 2
DAIL'S ZONE

1483
01:13:30,823 --> 01:13:31,908
It's 27 minutes. It's similar.

1484
01:13:31,991 --> 01:13:33,910
-[host] There are two Time Cases...
-A bit longer.

1485
01:13:33,993 --> 01:13:35,745
-...in Zone 2.
-[Ddolddol] No. 4 is a bit shorter.

1486
01:13:35,828 --> 01:13:36,871
-I'll check.
-Okay.

1487
01:13:36,954 --> 01:13:38,873
ZONE 5
PANI BOTTLE'S ZONE

1488
01:13:38,956 --> 01:13:42,376
[host] Zone 5's slots
have increased to three.

1489
01:13:42,960 --> 01:13:44,754
-So three slots in Zone 5?
-[Joonsu] Here.

1490
01:13:44,837 --> 01:13:47,089
Then we'd better move one
from here to there.

1491
01:13:47,173 --> 01:13:48,883
[Dail] But that's far.

1492
01:13:48,966 --> 01:13:50,968
It's better to move it somewhere closer.

1493
01:13:51,052 --> 01:13:53,763
-That zone already has three slots.
-[Dail] We can make it three here too.

1494
01:13:53,846 --> 01:13:55,181
There shouldn't be three here.

1495
01:13:55,264 --> 01:13:57,141
Otherwise, the cases might end up here.

1496
01:13:57,224 --> 01:13:59,602
There has to be only one zone
with three slots.

1497
01:13:59,685 --> 01:14:01,979
[Dail] So, put two here.

1498
01:14:02,063 --> 01:14:03,606
[Ddolddol] No,
there shouldn't be three here.

1499
01:14:03,689 --> 01:14:06,609
The cases might end up here.
We should block that in the first place.

1500
01:14:06,692 --> 01:14:09,278
[Dail] I couldn't understand it.

1501
01:14:09,362 --> 01:14:10,571
Because either way,

1502
01:14:10,655 --> 01:14:12,657
Pani's zone is far from Jieun's.

1503
01:14:12,740 --> 01:14:15,284
Jieun would go to somewhere closer
for an attack.

1504
01:14:15,868 --> 01:14:18,204
Then shouldn't we block this spot

1505
01:14:18,287 --> 01:14:21,540
to make Jieun go back and forth farther?

1506
01:14:21,624 --> 01:14:24,210
What's the point of blocking it here?

1507
01:14:24,293 --> 01:14:26,003
-[Pani Bottle] What's with No. 5?
-Move it fast.

1508
01:14:26,087 --> 01:14:27,755
-Let's move No. 5. Hurry.
-Move No. 5.

1509
01:14:29,090 --> 01:14:30,424
[Pani Bottle] Are there two No. 5s?

1510
01:14:30,508 --> 01:14:32,009
-[exclaims]
-[Pani Bottle] Why?

1511
01:14:32,802 --> 01:14:34,512
[Dail] I didn't say it,
but I thought to myself,

1512
01:14:34,595 --> 01:14:36,055
"I can't believe him."

1513
01:14:36,138 --> 01:14:38,432
Even while helping us,
he's making a backup plan.

1514
01:14:38,516 --> 01:14:40,893
I can't believe Pani Bottle.

1515
01:14:40,977 --> 01:14:42,687
He's looking for a way
to survive alone now?

1516
01:14:43,270 --> 01:14:44,271
I still enjoyed it.

1517
01:14:44,355 --> 01:14:46,565
Even if I messed up,
I wouldn't get eliminated.

1518
01:14:48,818 --> 01:14:51,153
[Ddolddol] Put it here,
and don't touch it at all.

1519
01:14:51,237 --> 01:14:52,655
[Pani Bottle] We need to spread out now.

1520
01:14:52,738 --> 01:14:54,448
[Ddolddol] Don't touch No. 5
and spread out.

1521
01:14:54,532 --> 01:14:57,576
-[host] Zone 2 now has three slots.
-Split up...

1522
01:14:58,077 --> 01:14:59,203
-[Ddolddol sighs]
-[Pani Bottle] Zone 2?

1523
01:14:59,286 --> 01:15:02,790
NO. 4 CASE TIMER

1524
01:15:03,499 --> 01:15:04,500
[Pani Bottle] Why?

1525
01:15:04,583 --> 01:15:07,545
INCLUDING TRAVEL TIME,
EXCEEDED THREE MINUTES

1526
01:15:08,546 --> 01:15:10,798
-So we could put several there as well?
-[Pani Bottle groans]

1527
01:15:10,881 --> 01:15:12,174
Why would it increase to three?

1528
01:15:12,258 --> 01:15:14,510
[Ddolddol] I don't know.
It must've passed three minutes.

1529
01:15:15,011 --> 01:15:16,345
[Pani Bottle sighs] Shit.

1530
01:15:16,429 --> 01:15:18,180
I didn't see this coming.

1531
01:15:18,264 --> 01:15:20,433
I don't think I'll be eliminated.

1532
01:15:20,516 --> 01:15:23,811
I'm afraid someone on my side
might end up getting eliminated.

1533
01:15:23,894 --> 01:15:25,229
Let's go all out, no matter what.

1534
01:15:27,982 --> 01:15:30,568
ZONE 6 IS STILL EMPTY

1535
01:15:30,651 --> 01:15:31,736
ZONE 6 SHIN JIEUN

1536
01:15:31,819 --> 01:15:34,613
CASES ARE CLUSTERED IN ZONES 2, 3, 5

1537
01:15:36,490 --> 01:15:37,658
[Jieun] Zone 3...

1538
01:15:44,999 --> 01:15:47,418
-[Joonsu] What are you looking for?
-I'm not looking for anything.

1539
01:15:47,501 --> 01:15:50,963
I believe they're not letting me
know the time left on purpose

1540
01:15:51,047 --> 01:15:52,673
by not placing any cases.

1541
01:15:52,757 --> 01:15:55,384
I was supposed to know the timers

1542
01:15:55,468 --> 01:15:57,636
so I could make predictions.

1543
01:15:57,720 --> 01:16:01,849
But with no cases in my zone,
I had no way of knowing.

1544
01:16:01,932 --> 01:16:03,809
[Joonsu] Yes, that makes sense.

1545
01:16:03,893 --> 01:16:05,227
Be careful.

1546
01:16:05,311 --> 01:16:07,730
[Jieun] Just let me know the time
once you find out.

1547
01:16:08,314 --> 01:16:10,858
Or you can move my case over later.

1548
01:16:12,818 --> 01:16:14,487
I couldn't communicate with him.

1549
01:16:16,197 --> 01:16:17,782
You know how many minutes are left?

1550
01:16:17,865 --> 01:16:19,366
-The case?
-I don't know.

1551
01:16:21,535 --> 01:16:22,536
Damn it...

1552
01:16:27,208 --> 01:16:29,085
[Joonsu] Where on earth are they?

1553
01:16:30,294 --> 01:16:31,962
JOONSU IS LOOKING FOR THE SPAWNED CASES

1554
01:16:34,048 --> 01:16:35,049
[object scrapes]

1555
01:16:37,218 --> 01:16:39,053
[groans] Where did they hide it?

1556
01:16:39,678 --> 01:16:40,679
Unbelievable.

1557
01:16:42,014 --> 01:16:44,433
[alarm blaring]

1558
01:16:44,517 --> 01:16:47,561
[host] A new case
has been added to the Maze.

1559
01:16:47,645 --> 01:16:48,813
A NEW CASE IN THE MAZE

1560
01:16:48,896 --> 01:16:52,483
Only the first two arriving players
can claim the cases.

1561
01:16:52,566 --> 01:16:53,567
[Pani Bottle] Fuck.

1562
01:16:54,777 --> 01:16:57,196
The second I heard the announcement,
I began running.

1563
01:16:57,279 --> 01:17:00,741
If Jieun happens to find them in the maze,

1564
01:17:00,825 --> 01:17:03,077
my plan's done for, so I ran like hell.

1565
01:17:15,047 --> 01:17:18,551
DAIL ARRIVES AT THE MAZE FIRST

1566
01:17:19,677 --> 01:17:21,804
[Dail] I ran like crazy because of this.

1567
01:17:23,556 --> 01:17:24,682
I found it.

1568
01:17:26,225 --> 01:17:28,769
I quickly got in and picked up the case.

1569
01:17:28,853 --> 01:17:31,814
[Ddolddol] Add this to my zone.
One more. Give it to me.

1570
01:17:32,523 --> 01:17:33,983
PRISON MATES GET SPAWNED CASES

1571
01:17:34,066 --> 01:17:35,192
[Pani Bottle] Look at the time.

1572
01:17:42,950 --> 01:17:45,369
ZONE 3
JOONSU'S ZONE

1573
01:17:45,452 --> 01:17:46,453
[Ddolddol] Look at this.

1574
01:17:47,454 --> 01:17:50,833
-[Pani Bottle] There's 13 minutes.
-Okay. No. 7 has 13 minutes.

1575
01:17:50,916 --> 01:17:52,543
JIEUN WAS MONITORING THE PRISON MEMBERS

1576
01:17:52,626 --> 01:17:55,629
[host] There are two Time Cases in Zone 3.

1577
01:17:55,713 --> 01:17:56,755
Zone 3?

1578
01:18:03,888 --> 01:18:05,389
DDOLDDOL AND PANI BOTTLE'S
SUSPICIOUS MOVES

1579
01:18:05,472 --> 01:18:07,474
-[Ddolddol] Hold on.
-[Pani Bottle] Let's go to Dail.

1580
01:18:07,558 --> 01:18:08,726
SPOTS SHIN JIEUN

1581
01:18:09,560 --> 01:18:10,769
I need to check the timer on No. 8.

1582
01:18:10,853 --> 01:18:11,854
PRISON MEMBERS BECOME FRANTIC

1583
01:18:11,937 --> 01:18:14,982
ZONE 4
DDOLDDOL'S ZONE

1584
01:18:18,903 --> 01:18:21,071
[Dail] I saw it had barely any time left.

1585
01:18:21,155 --> 01:18:23,908
I passed Case No. 8 to the other two.

1586
01:18:23,991 --> 01:18:25,868
-What I brought over is No. 8.
-No. 8.

1587
01:18:25,951 --> 01:18:26,952
Just focus on that.

1588
01:18:27,036 --> 01:18:28,662
We need to get this done now.

1589
01:18:28,746 --> 01:18:30,915
-[Ddolddol] What?
-If I cut three minutes, it becomes six.

1590
01:18:30,998 --> 01:18:31,999
So we have to do it now.

1591
01:18:32,082 --> 01:18:34,084
I'll bring it when it's almost a minute.

1592
01:18:34,168 --> 01:18:35,419
PANI BOTTLE CAN ATTACK NO. 8?

1593
01:18:35,502 --> 01:18:37,504
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1594
01:18:38,130 --> 01:18:40,424
JIEUN STAYS CALM

1595
01:18:41,550 --> 01:18:43,636
[Jieun] I thought they had
the upper hand in location

1596
01:18:43,719 --> 01:18:47,514
when it came to finding them,

1597
01:18:47,598 --> 01:18:51,352
so I kept thinking about
how I should deal with it.

1598
01:18:52,853 --> 01:18:55,189
I decided to focus on defense first.

1599
01:18:55,272 --> 01:18:57,399
SHIN JIEUN

1600
01:18:57,483 --> 01:19:00,152
SHE LEFT HER POSITION ON PURPOSE
IN ROUND 1

1601
01:19:00,236 --> 01:19:01,445
SHIN JIEUN

1602
01:19:01,528 --> 01:19:05,074
JIEUN STAYS AWAY FROM HER ZONE ON PURPOSE

1603
01:19:05,157 --> 01:19:06,867
[Pani Bottle] Now six minutes? Or five?

1604
01:19:06,951 --> 01:19:08,953
-We can't have it blow up in our hands.
-Right.

1605
01:19:09,036 --> 01:19:10,788
Go slow and I'll use it right away.

1606
01:19:10,871 --> 01:19:12,206
-Right now?
-[Ddolddol] No.

1607
01:19:12,289 --> 01:19:13,916
Set it off 15 seconds later.

1608
01:19:13,999 --> 01:19:16,085
Okay, 15, 14, 13...

1609
01:19:16,168 --> 01:19:17,211
DDOLDDOL MOVES CASE NO. 8

1610
01:19:17,294 --> 01:19:18,587
Twelve, eleven, ten,

1611
01:19:18,671 --> 01:19:20,005
"PANI BOTTLE GOES TO DEALER ROOM"

1612
01:19:20,089 --> 01:19:22,591
nine, eight, seven...

1613
01:19:23,175 --> 01:19:24,385
...three,

1614
01:19:24,468 --> 01:19:25,552
two,

1615
01:19:25,636 --> 01:19:27,096
one.

1616
01:19:27,179 --> 01:19:29,056
ZONE 6
JIEUN'S ZONE

1617
01:19:30,683 --> 01:19:33,727
[host] There are two Time Cases in Zone 6.

1618
01:19:36,355 --> 01:19:41,235
My plan was to act clueless the whole time
and strike at the last second.

1619
01:19:41,318 --> 01:19:42,736
So I took off running.

1620
01:19:42,820 --> 01:19:43,862
DEALER ROOM

1621
01:19:43,946 --> 01:19:45,781
[dealer] Would you like to use an item?

1622
01:19:45,864 --> 01:19:48,033
I'll take three minutes away
on Case No. 8.

1623
01:19:48,575 --> 01:19:52,037
[dealer] Case No. 8's timer
will be reduced by three minutes.

1624
01:19:53,872 --> 01:19:56,166
[host] An item was applied to Case No. 8.

1625
01:19:56,750 --> 01:19:58,544
[Joonsu] Jieun, no! Damn it.

1626
01:20:03,757 --> 01:20:05,426
[case explodes]

1627
01:20:06,844 --> 01:20:09,972
[host] Shin Jieun's Time Case
has exploded.

1628
01:20:10,514 --> 01:20:11,515
[Jieun] What happened?

1629
01:20:12,308 --> 01:20:15,144
I heard that my case... [chuckling]

1630
01:20:15,227 --> 01:20:16,437
...had suddenly exploded.

1631
01:20:17,187 --> 01:20:18,314
DEALER ROOM
1 MINUTE AGO

1632
01:20:18,397 --> 01:20:20,149
Would you like to use an item?

1633
01:20:20,232 --> 01:20:22,484
I'll take three minutes away
on Case No. 8.

1634
01:20:23,193 --> 01:20:25,029
PANI BOTTLE CAME BACK RIGHT AWAY

1635
01:20:25,112 --> 01:20:27,156
I'll take three minutes away
from Case No. 8.

1636
01:20:27,239 --> 01:20:28,532
USED THE NO. 8 CARD AGAIN

1637
01:20:28,615 --> 01:20:30,534
In the middle of the game,

1638
01:20:30,617 --> 01:20:31,910
Joonsu came over to me.

1639
01:20:31,994 --> 01:20:32,995
So...

1640
01:20:34,121 --> 01:20:35,247
BEFORE ROUND 2 BEGAN

1641
01:20:38,834 --> 01:20:42,296
Round 2 is going to be all about politics.

1642
01:20:42,379 --> 01:20:43,964
We need to take them out here.

1643
01:20:44,965 --> 01:20:47,259
-There's no reason to keep them around.
-[Joonsu] I agree.

1644
01:20:47,760 --> 01:20:48,969
Forget about alliances.

1645
01:20:49,053 --> 01:20:52,514
I was in a position
where I could be betrayed at any moment.

1646
01:20:52,598 --> 01:20:55,893
[host] The players Shin Jieun chose
as her Death Match opponents are...

1647
01:20:55,976 --> 01:20:57,811
Lee Joonsu.

1648
01:20:57,895 --> 01:20:59,063
-How many did you find?
-[Joonsu] Three.

1649
01:20:59,146 --> 01:21:01,690
-[Jieun] Give me one. Give me one.
-[Joonsu] I'll find one.

1650
01:21:01,774 --> 01:21:03,400
JOONSU WAS HESITANT

1651
01:21:03,484 --> 01:21:04,777
[Jieun] Did you hear me?

1652
01:21:05,903 --> 01:21:08,113
[Joonsu] I couldn't stop suspecting Jieun.

1653
01:21:08,697 --> 01:21:10,741
I was afraid I'd get betrayed again.

1654
01:21:10,824 --> 01:21:13,577
I figured, to survive,
I'd have to betray her first.

1655
01:21:13,660 --> 01:21:14,787
I had to prove

1656
01:21:15,621 --> 01:21:17,998
to the guys that I could be useful.

1657
01:21:18,082 --> 01:21:19,124
I found one.

1658
01:21:19,208 --> 01:21:20,292
Thank you.

1659
01:21:20,376 --> 01:21:22,419
-Hey, take this.
-Thank you.

1660
01:21:22,503 --> 01:21:26,006
Luckily, the two cards
Joonsu gave me in a hurry

1661
01:21:26,090 --> 01:21:27,466
happened to be two eights.

1662
01:21:27,549 --> 01:21:28,884
When I saw that,

1663
01:21:28,967 --> 01:21:31,637
I was completely relieved.

1664
01:21:31,720 --> 01:21:33,889
This time, I knew I was safe. Okay.

1665
01:21:33,972 --> 01:21:35,766
The game was pretty much over then.

1666
01:21:35,849 --> 01:21:38,560
I'll climb back up.
I'll survive and make it back.

1667
01:21:38,644 --> 01:21:40,104
That's all I could think of.

1668
01:21:41,021 --> 01:21:43,524
-Another No. 8?
-Yes, minus three minutes.

1669
01:21:43,607 --> 01:21:47,194
[dealer] All right. Case No. 8's timer
will be reduced by three minutes.

1670
01:21:48,112 --> 01:21:50,322
[host] An item was applied to Case No. 8.

1671
01:21:52,157 --> 01:21:54,701
-Shin Jieun's Time Case...
-[sighs]

1672
01:21:55,202 --> 01:21:56,578
...has exploded.

1673
01:22:01,792 --> 01:22:05,045
[Jieun] I think
I'd already come to terms with it.

1674
01:22:06,004 --> 01:22:07,756
[host] "Time Case" is over.

1675
01:22:08,674 --> 01:22:11,927
But getting eliminated first
is a little too much.

1676
01:22:12,553 --> 01:22:14,471
[chuckling] I'm kind of mad.

1677
01:22:15,264 --> 01:22:18,225
[host] We will announce the results
of the Death Match.

1678
01:22:18,308 --> 01:22:20,394
Everyone, please gather in the Main Hall.

1679
01:22:22,980 --> 01:22:27,025
The contestants eliminated from Deadly Tag

1680
01:22:27,109 --> 01:22:28,360
after today's Death Match

1681
01:22:31,155 --> 01:22:32,281
are Gyeong Sujin

1682
01:22:32,990 --> 01:22:35,242
and Shin Jieun.

1683
01:22:36,493 --> 01:22:38,704
Gyeong Sujin and Shin Jieun,

1684
01:22:38,787 --> 01:22:42,624
please exit the area immediately.

1685
01:22:42,708 --> 01:22:43,709
[sighs]

1686
01:22:43,792 --> 01:22:45,752
[♪ pensive music playing]

1687
01:22:47,004 --> 01:22:48,005
Eliminated players

1688
01:22:49,047 --> 01:22:52,676
will not be able to return to Deadly Tag.

1689
01:22:57,473 --> 01:22:59,057
I'll get going.

1690
01:22:59,141 --> 01:23:00,142
Good job, everyone.

1691
01:23:01,185 --> 01:23:02,644
[Sujin] I wish you the best of luck.

1692
01:23:03,353 --> 01:23:04,938
-Good work.
-[Sujin] Bye.

1693
01:23:05,689 --> 01:23:07,065
-Take care.
-[player] Keep in touch.

1694
01:23:07,149 --> 01:23:09,693
-[Jieun] I've grown so attached now.
-I know.

1695
01:23:09,776 --> 01:23:11,612
Because of the last 10 seconds...

1696
01:23:11,695 --> 01:23:12,696
[Pani Bottle sighs]

1697
01:23:17,993 --> 01:23:19,036
[Sujin sighs heavily]

1698
01:23:21,079 --> 01:23:23,457
-[Jieun] You did so great.
-[Sujin] It's such a shame.

1699
01:23:23,540 --> 01:23:26,210
-It's such a shame. [sighs]
-[Jieun] It really is.

1700
01:23:28,795 --> 01:23:33,592
I was really motivated and driven.

1701
01:23:34,343 --> 01:23:37,304
I feel like I went through
this prison life...

1702
01:23:37,387 --> 01:23:40,724
-There's no one.
-...more intensely than anyone else.

1703
01:23:41,391 --> 01:23:43,560
-[Ddolddol] Want me to clean this up?
-No, it's fine.

1704
01:23:43,644 --> 01:23:46,522
I think the game itself was a lot of fun.

1705
01:23:47,147 --> 01:23:50,400
This experience made me understand

1706
01:23:50,484 --> 01:23:52,069
how important politics are...

1707
01:23:52,152 --> 01:23:53,153
-[explodes]
-[yelps]

1708
01:23:53,237 --> 01:23:56,448
...in a survival game.

1709
01:23:57,366 --> 01:23:58,700
SUJIN GAVE IT HER BEST AT EVERY MOMENT

1710
01:23:58,784 --> 01:23:59,952
What's with them?

1711
01:24:03,372 --> 01:24:07,084
I think I'm actually a very soft person

1712
01:24:07,167 --> 01:24:09,586
deep down inside.

1713
01:24:09,670 --> 01:24:11,296
But as I played this game...

1714
01:24:12,339 --> 01:24:15,592
-Run!
-I wanted to show my cool and tough side.

1715
01:24:15,676 --> 01:24:19,513
I wanted to do whatever it took
to win by being selfish

1716
01:24:20,180 --> 01:24:21,598
or by betraying others.

1717
01:24:21,682 --> 01:24:23,559
I wanted to show that side of me.

1718
01:24:23,642 --> 01:24:26,770
But while playing the game, I found myself

1719
01:24:26,853 --> 01:24:29,606
just having fun
and getting along with everyone.

1720
01:24:30,315 --> 01:24:31,316
[chuckles]

1721
01:24:34,194 --> 01:24:36,572
Get him, get him!

1722
01:24:37,739 --> 01:24:38,740
[grunts]

1723
01:24:39,825 --> 01:24:42,244
I enjoyed spending time

1724
01:24:42,327 --> 01:24:44,746
with such wonderful people
on this program.

1725
01:24:44,830 --> 01:24:47,040
[♪ emotional music playing]

1726
01:24:47,124 --> 01:24:48,625
I had such a great time.

1727
01:24:50,127 --> 01:24:51,545
I'm sad that it's over,

1728
01:24:52,337 --> 01:24:54,840
but when you think about it,
there's only one winner

1729
01:24:54,923 --> 01:24:57,050
and I just got eliminated a little sooner.

1730
01:24:57,134 --> 01:25:00,512
They'll get eliminated one by one
in their own time.

1731
01:25:00,596 --> 01:25:02,222
I hope they do their best out there.

1732
01:25:02,306 --> 01:25:06,810
I'm leaving with some regrets,
but I'll get going.

1733
01:25:08,979 --> 01:25:14,318
FINAL ELIMINATIONS
GYEONG SUJIN, SHIN JIEUN

1734
01:25:16,069 --> 01:25:18,488
[Pani Bottle sighs]
So this is the Main Hall.

1735
01:25:18,572 --> 01:25:19,865
Let's do a toast.

1736
01:25:19,948 --> 01:25:21,700
-[Ddolddol] Good work.
-Cheers.

1737
01:25:24,578 --> 01:25:25,662
[exhales]

1738
01:25:25,746 --> 01:25:27,247
Mmm!

1739
01:25:29,124 --> 01:25:31,001
Are you going to bed, Horseking?

1740
01:25:31,918 --> 01:25:33,337
-I don't know.
-[Pani Bottle] Okay.

1741
01:25:33,420 --> 01:25:34,463
AWKWARD RESPONSE FROM OTHERS

1742
01:25:34,546 --> 01:25:35,964
-[Ddolddol] See you tomorrow.
-Good night.

1743
01:25:36,548 --> 01:25:38,884
[Ddolddol] I don't think
we're exactly welcome.

1744
01:25:38,967 --> 01:25:40,510
I don't think we're exactly welcome.

1745
01:25:41,094 --> 01:25:43,805
Even better.
This is exactly what I wanted.

1746
01:25:43,889 --> 01:25:46,642
They reacted like, "There are
more survivors than I expected."

1747
01:25:46,725 --> 01:25:48,477
Like, "Get a load of these punks."

1748
01:25:48,560 --> 01:25:49,561
I love it.

1749
01:25:50,604 --> 01:25:51,688
Let's crush them all.

1750
01:25:52,731 --> 01:25:54,316
[Pani Bottle and Ddolddol laughing]

1751
01:25:54,399 --> 01:25:56,068
[Ddolddol] Because they're all rivals.

1752
01:25:56,151 --> 01:25:57,444
[chuckles]

1753
01:25:57,944 --> 01:25:59,821
[Pani Bottle]
The three of us had this mindset

1754
01:25:59,905 --> 01:26:01,531
that we'd return and crush everyone.

1755
01:26:01,615 --> 01:26:03,575
[Dail] I don't think anyone could beat us.

1756
01:26:03,659 --> 01:26:06,203
I think the entire dynamic will change.

1757
01:26:10,165 --> 01:26:13,251
[distorted voice] Yeah,
tear each other apart and fight it out.

1758
01:26:13,335 --> 01:26:15,295
[laughing maniacally]

1759
01:26:18,507 --> 01:26:20,092
[Pani Bottle sighs frustratedly]

1760
01:26:20,175 --> 01:26:21,677
God damn it!

1761
01:26:21,760 --> 01:26:22,928
This is making me angry.

1762
01:26:23,011 --> 01:26:24,971
The prison team is too intimidating.

1763
01:26:25,055 --> 01:26:26,306
The prison crew is insane.

1764
01:26:26,390 --> 01:26:27,641
[Dail] I want to punch them.

1765
01:26:27,724 --> 01:26:28,725
It's fun.

1766
01:26:28,809 --> 01:26:30,102
It's not fun for me.

1767
01:26:30,185 --> 01:26:32,896
[Jimin] The prison team seemed
to be banding together so closely.

1768
01:26:32,979 --> 01:26:34,856
It's intimidating, but at the same time...

1769
01:26:34,940 --> 01:26:38,026
[Horseking] The prison team's getting
a little too full of themselves.

1770
01:26:38,527 --> 01:26:42,239
[host] This Main Match
is a team competition called "Kingmaker."

1771
01:26:42,781 --> 01:26:46,368
[Dail] The prison team's getting
a little too full of themselves.

1772
01:26:46,451 --> 01:26:47,911
[Pani Bottle]
Keep the strong players in check.

1773
01:26:47,994 --> 01:26:49,996
[Ddolddol] Yuk Junseo, Horseking?
Tag them, no matter what.

1774
01:26:50,706 --> 01:26:51,790
[Junseo] Catch them!

1775
01:26:51,873 --> 01:26:54,501
[Horseking]
Run like your life depends on it.

1776
01:26:55,085 --> 01:26:57,212
-[Ddolddol] Horseking is here!
-[Dail] Where did he go?

1777
01:26:57,796 --> 01:26:58,964
[Dail] The game is ours.

1778
01:26:59,047 --> 01:27:01,174
[Junseo] What? [groans]

1779
01:27:01,258 --> 01:27:02,592
[Horseking] I'm confused.

1780
01:27:03,218 --> 01:27:04,219
[Junseo] Fuck.

1781
01:27:04,302 --> 01:27:05,470
[Ddolddol] Oh my, look at this.

1782
01:27:05,554 --> 01:27:07,639
Horseking and Yuk Junseo
have been crippled.

1783
01:27:07,723 --> 01:27:10,600
[host] The contestants eliminated
from Deadly Tag are...

1784
01:27:12,728 --> 01:27:14,730
[♪ ominous music playing]

1785
01:27:32,622 --> 01:27:34,624
Translated by Youji Kim
